{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M256myJ4LYb6n1SPHTVU5A","type":"tool_result","content":"191:drive reads an item's latest records and a forge's own check conclusions\n192-and performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\n193-valid approval refuses by name and runs nothing; no passing build bound to\n194-that approval runs build; a passing build with the forge green on the\n195-branch head (polled for a bound, not the manifest) runs verify; a passing\n196-verify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\n197-and stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\n198-nothing. A record build or verify writes that is not pass is counseled (counsel,\n199-issue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\n200-so its .filed marker exists in time to be committed alongside it; drive\n201-then commits the stage record and the counsel record together -- each\n202-with its own log and marker -- with `git commit --only`, never sweeping\n203-the index, and pushes; a push a divergent remote rejects\n204-is retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit`, never a rebase,\n205-since the record already names the commit's sha. drive writes no record\n206-of its own: a second run in the same state repeats the same step or the\n207-same stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\n208-included, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\n209-worktree or a fresh one. See issue #84's lane for the full rules it\n210-enforces.\n211-\n212---until-ready (issue #100's own followups) repeats step-and-wait --\n213-step, the forge poll already inside a step, step again -- in the same\n214-process, rather than making the caller invoke drive again after every\n215-passing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\n216-own account (a refusal, a halted or failed or refused record, or the\n217-forge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\n218-the same step would print without the flag. Without --until-ready,\n219-drive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n220-\n221-ledger reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d","uuid":"757dc209-94b5-4dc2-b6bd-5f1adb7ffe25","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:46:27.630Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"191:drive reads an item's latest records and a forge's own check conclusions\n192-and performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\n193-valid approval refuses by name and runs nothing; no passing build bound to\n194-that approval runs build; a passing build with the forge green on the\n195-branch head (polled for a bound, not the manifest) runs verify; a passing\n196-verify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\n197-and stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\n198-nothing. A record build or verify writes that is not pass is counseled (counsel,\n199-issue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\n200-so its .filed marker exists in time to be committed alongside it; drive\n201-then commits the stage record and the counsel record together -- each\n202-with its own log and marker -- with `git commit --only`, never sweeping\n203-the index, and pushes; a push a divergent remote rejects\n204-is retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit`, never a rebase,\n205-since the record already names the commit's sha. drive writes no record\n206-of its own: a second run in the same state repeats the same step or the\n207-same stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\n208-included, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\n209-worktree or a fresh one. See issue #84's lane for the full rules it\n210-enforces.\n211-\n212---until-ready (issue #100's own followups) repeats step-and-wait --\n213-step, the forge poll already inside a step, step again -- in the same\n214-process, rather than making the caller invoke drive again after every\n215-passing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\n216-own account (a refusal, a halted or failed or refused record, or the\n217-forge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\n218-the same step would print without the flag. Without --until-ready,\n219-drive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n220-\n221-ledger reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
