{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9bXA5QLomzkzZL5w5NV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X6i2kU59apsHFaUKnmi33a","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo","old_string":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log, last_at = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since(last_at or info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")","new_string":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since_last_event(events, info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":174277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d","uuid":"074fd186-7657-4227-8f11-8d4536590d47","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:52:55.900Z","request_id":"req_011Cf9bX9MyuhvCDQkdvvCGJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X6i2kU59apsHFaUKnmi33a":{"file_path":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo","old_string":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log, last_at = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since(last_at or info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")","new_string":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since_last_event(events, info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6i2kU59apsHFaUKnmi33a","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d","uuid":"aaeabddb-ad62-4579-b623-a16c2b639ef8","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:52:55.936Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo","oldString":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log, last_at = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since(last_at or info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")","newString":"        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since_last_event(events, info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")","originalFile":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n\n    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n    attavo spec-gate [N]\n    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n    attavo approval-status [N]\n    attavo build [N]\n    attavo verify [N]\n    attavo file-findings [N]\n    attavo file-stops [N]\n    attavo counsel [N]\n    attavo record-only\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready] [--recover]\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n                             heading when a build failed after running\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                             never refused\n  5. no-invocation-lacks-record  every <stage>-NN.started marker under\n                             paths.records names a live invocation (its pid\n                             on its host) or has a <stage>-NN.json beside\n                             it -- a marker naming neither is an invocation\n                             that began and died with nothing to show for\n                             it (issue #151). Refuses when the manifest\n                             carries no [drive].stall_after_s, since a\n                             hung invocation cannot then be told from a\n                             running one.\n\nNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\nblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\nis done.\n\nspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\none enforces.\n\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\ndeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\nwhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\nnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\nbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\nunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\nbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\nenforces.\n\nverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\nstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\na tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\nline per check as \"<name> <conclusion>\". verify runs it on the build\nrecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\nskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\nadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\ncalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\n[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\nthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\nfindings and its declared \"reports\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\nbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\nresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\ncarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\ncarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\nthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\nrefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\nretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\nfull rules both enforce.\n\nfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\nissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\nclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\nlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\nbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\nfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\nthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\ncommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\nnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\nempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\ncould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n\ncounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\nwhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\npoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\napproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\n[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\nread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\nclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\nitem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\nroot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\nsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\nstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\ncitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\ndiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\n(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\nand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\nthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\ntranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\ncaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\nwritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\nrecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\nenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\n\nrecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\npaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\ncheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\nguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\ncopy of the check.\n\nattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\nverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha\nnames the latest approval, and the verify's build_sha names that build --\na re-approval after a build must force a re-run of what changed. With no\nN given it derives the item from the record paths HEAD's merge commit\ntouched under paths.records/<N>/, not from a branch name, which a squash\nmerge discards and which names a forge's convention the product does not\nknow; more than one item derived is a refusal naming what it found. Zero\nis not a defect -- not every merge is an item merge -- exit 0, nothing\nprinted but a line saying so.\n\nattest never writes. On a coherent chain it prints the attestation\nstatement -- validating against schema/attestation.schema.json -- to\nstdout as JSON and exits 0: the item, its four records and their shas,\nand the commit the statement was computed at (sha and merge_sha are the\nsame commit here; on the merge group that commit is the one that lands).\nThe four stage records already under paths.records are the evidence for\nthat statement; a forge-specific template signs the printed JSON,\nunmodified, as the predicate, against the commit that lands, on the merge\ngroup -- and the signed bundle in the forge's attestation store is the\nseal over it. attest itself never signs anything and never talks to a\nsigning service. --partial (issue #67) is for a pull request, where the\nrecord a complete chain would need is the output of a later stage that is\nitself waiting on this check: a missing later record is \"not yet\" (exit\n0, naming the item and the stages present and absent, no statement\nprinted) rather than a refusal, while the two chain assertions -- build's\napproval_sha names the latest approval, verify's build_sha names the\nlatest build -- still run over whatever records exist. merge_group and a\npush to main still demand the whole chain. See issue #69's lane for the\nfull rules it enforces.\n\ndrive reads an item's latest records and a forge's own check conclusions\nand performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\nvalid approval refuses by name and runs nothing; no passing build bound to\nthat approval runs build; a passing build with the forge green on the\nbranch head (polled for a bound, not the manifest) runs verify; a passing\nverify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\nand stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\nnothing. A record build or verify writes that is not pass is counseled (counsel,\nissue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\nso its .filed marker exists in time to be committed alongside it; drive\nthen commits the stage record and the counsel record together -- each\nwith its own log and marker -- with `git commit --only`, never sweeping\nthe index, and pushes; a push a divergent remote rejects\nis retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit`, never a rebase,\nsince the record already names the commit's sha. drive writes no record\nof its own: a second run in the same state repeats the same step or the\nsame stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\nincluded, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\nworktree or a fresh one. See issue #84's lane for the full rules it\nenforces.\n\n--until-ready (issue #100's own followups) repeats step-and-wait --\nstep, the forge poll already inside a step, step again -- in the same\nprocess, rather than making the caller invoke drive again after every\npassing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\nown account (a refusal, a halted or failed or refused record, or the\nforge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\nthe same step would print without the flag. Without --until-ready,\ndrive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n\nBefore running build or verify, drive writes a <stage>-NN.started marker\n(at, host, pid, the sha it starts on) and commits and pushes it by itself,\nso the fact that this invocation began is on the branch before the\nadapter runs -- an invocation that dies with the process or hangs past\n[drive].stall_after_s leaves this marker with no record beside it, which\ndoctor's fifth proof names (issue #151). --recover reads every marker of\nan item with no record beside it: a dead pid (gone, or on another host)\nwrites a failed record, stop class died; a live one past the stall bound\nwith no newer event in its adapter's own events file is terminated and\nwritten up as class hung; a live one still inside the bound is left\nalone. Provenance product either way, the events tail as the log,\nwritten, committed, and pushed the same way any stage record is -- the\nnext ordinary drive call then reads that non-pass record and does what\nit always does with one. See issue #151's lane for the full rules it\nenforces.\n\nledger reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\npaths.records when N is omitted), it walks the commits from the item's\nfirst spec commit to its merge (the same derivation doctor's proof two\nand attest use) or to HEAD when the item has not merged, and prints one\nrow per act: the sha, the identity as git names it, and a class from a\nclosed list -- spec, amend, approve, launch, record, change, transport,\nmerge -- derived from who committed it and, for an approval, build, or\nverify record, what the record itself says. A summary line follows:\noperator acts (approve, amend, launch, transport, merge), product acts\n(record), executor commits (change), stops (non-pass records), and\nsince (the product version on the first record). A build or verify\nrecord's own commit, from before v0.18.0 gave the driver and the\nexecutor their own identities, prints as record-or-launch with a note,\ncounted toward neither total, rather than guessed. --json prints the\nrows and the summary as one object. See issue #128's lane for the full\nrules it enforces.\n\nstops reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\npaths.records when N is omitted), one row per non-pass build or verify\nrecord: the record, its stop's class, provenance, and detail, and the\nanswerer -- \"counsel:<verdict>\" when a counsel record read this exact\nstop, else \"person\" for a question, else \"guard\" for a class a guard\nalone raised (GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES), else \"none\". A record too old to\ncarry stop at all prints the doctor's own phrase for it, \"before stop\nwas recorded\", and is counted there rather than by class. Totals per\nclass (read from the build record schema's own enum, never retyped) and\nper answerer, plus the before-stop count, follow the rows. --json prints\nthe rows and the totals as one object. See issue #129's lane for the\nfull rules it enforces.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport fnmatch\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shlex\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nimport tomllib\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nMANIFEST = \"attavo.toml\"\nSTAGES = (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\")\nCRITERION_TIMEOUT = 120\nRECORD_RE = re.compile(r\"^([a-z]+)-([0-9]{2,})\\.json$\")\nBUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\nBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\nCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\nPRODUCT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n# issue #84: a constant the lane names, not a manifest key, until a tenant\n# disagrees -- how long drive gives a forge's checks room to conclude\n# before it gives up and stops rather than call a judge on a tree the\n# forge has not yet finished reading. Tenant zero's own checks conclude\n# about five minutes after a push; the default bound gives them room to\n# finish so a person is not the one re-running drive after CI, which is\n# exactly the transport act this lane retires. ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\n# and ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S, read at call time rather than once at\n# import, are for a test's own clock, not a tenant's -- there is no\n# manifest key for either.\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S = 600.0\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S = 20.0\n\n\ndef drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\ndef drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\nclass Proof:\n    def __init__(self, key: str, title: str) -> None:\n        self.key = key\n        self.title = title\n        self.holds = False\n        self.reason = \"\"\n        self.extra: dict = {}\n\n    def fail(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = False, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def hold(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = True, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"proof\": self.key, \"title\": self.title,\n                \"holds\": self.holds, \"reason\": self.reason, **self.extra}\n\n\ndef read_manifest(root: Path) -> dict | None:\n    path = root / MANIFEST\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return None\n    with path.open(\"rb\") as fh:\n        return tomllib.load(fh)\n\n\ndef git(root: Path, *args: str, env: dict | None = None) -> str:\n    out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *args],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\n    if out.returncode != 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(out.stderr.strip() or \"git failed\")\n    return out.stdout\n\n\ndef product_version() -> str:\n    \"\"\"What the running program is. Three fallbacks, in order, and never an\n    exception -- this runs inside write_record, after the work it\n    describes already happened, and a raise here would lose the record\n    for an invocation that already ran:\n\n      1. ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION, when the environment sets it. The forge\n         action sets this from its own ref (action.yml, not here -- this\n         function stays forge-agnostic).\n      2. git describe --tags --always --dirty against PRODUCT_ROOT: a\n         tagged release reports its tag, a checkout reports its commit,\n         a dirty tree says so.\n      3. \"unknown\", when PRODUCT_ROOT is not a git repository at all --\n         the case for a forge that extracts this action from a tarball\n         rather than a git checkout, which is exactly when (1) is\n         expected to already have supplied the answer.\n\n    Distinct from the tenant's product_pin -- an operator running a\n    checkout, which is how every build and verify have actually been run\n    so far, bypasses the pin entirely (issue #49).\"\"\"\n    env = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION\")\n    if env:\n        return env\n    try:\n        return git(PRODUCT_ROOT, \"describe\", \"--tags\", \"--always\", \"--dirty\").strip()\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return \"unknown\"\n\n\ndef now_iso() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef derive_item_id(root: Path) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"ATTAVO_ITEM first, not last: a rejection fixture's own item id must\n    win over whatever attavo/N-* branch the enclosing tenant repository\n    happens to be checked out on -- the common case is doctor running from\n    a real item's own branch, where a fallback-only env var would never be\n    consulted at all and every gate fixture would silently resolve to the\n    real item instead of its own.\"\"\"\n    env_item = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_ITEM\")\n    if env_item:\n        return env_item\n    out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    branch = out.stdout.strip()\n    m = re.match(r\"^attavo/(\\d+)-\", branch)\n    return m.group(1) if m else None\n\n\ndef fixture_item_id(fixture: Path) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The one item id under a rejection fixture's own paths.specs, so the\n    doctor can export it as ATTAVO_ITEM: a fixture carries no attavo/N-*\n    branch for a gate command with no argument to derive from otherwise.\"\"\"\n    fm = read_manifest(fixture)\n    specs_rel = ((fm or {}).get(\"paths\") or {}).get(\"specs\")\n    if not specs_rel:\n        return None\n    specs_dir = fixture / specs_rel\n    if not specs_dir.is_dir():\n        return None\n    items = sorted(p.name for p in specs_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir())\n    return items[0] if len(items) == 1 else None\n\n\nclass ShallowCheckoutError(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef last_commit_touching(root: Path, relpath: str) -> str | None:\n    shallow = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"rev-parse\", \"--is-shallow-repository\"],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if shallow.stdout.strip() == \"true\":\n        raise ShallowCheckoutError(\n            \"shallow checkout: git log -1 -- <path> returns HEAD for every path on a \"\n            \"shallow clone; check out with fetch-depth: 0\")\n    out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", relpath],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    sha = out.stdout.strip()\n    return sha or None\n\n\n# --- record files: <stage>-NN.json, one per attempt, never overwritten ---\n\nSCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR = PRODUCT_ROOT / \"schema\" / \"records\"\n\n\ndef stage_schema(stage: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"schema/records/<stage>.schema.json -- this repository's own\n    declaration of that stage's record shape (issue #60). The only\n    artifact the outbound contract needs; there is no accessor for it\n    beyond reading the file.\"\"\"\n    return json.loads((SCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR / f\"{stage}.schema.json\").read_text())\n\n\ndef schema_id_version(schema: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The trailing integer of a schema's $id (\".../records/build/2\" -> 2)\n    -- the single place a record shape's version lives. write_record reads\n    this at call time rather than carrying its own copy, so the version it\n    stamps cannot drift from what the schema declares (issue #60).\"\"\"\n    return int(schema[\"$id\"].rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1])\n\n\nclass RecordItemMismatch(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"A record's item field disagrees with the directory it was read\n    from (issue #60, acceptance 5) -- a misfiled or copied record, refused\n    rather than trusted.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _load_record(path: Path, item_id: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The one place in this repository that turns a record file's bytes\n    into a dict (issue #60, acceptance 6). Defaults record_version to 1\n    when absent -- version 1 is every record written before this release\n    and is never migrated -- and fills item from the directory when\n    absent; refuses when a present item disagrees with it.\"\"\"\n    data = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    data.setdefault(\"record_version\", 1)\n    item = data.get(\"item\")\n    if item is None:\n        data[\"item\"] = item_id\n    elif item != item_id:\n        raise RecordItemMismatch(\n            f\"{path}: item {item!r} disagrees with its directory {item_id!r}\")\n    return data\n\n\ndef parse_attempts(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict[int, dict]:\n    attempts: dict[int, dict] = {}\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return attempts\n    for f in records_dir.glob(f\"{stage}-*.json\"):\n        m = RECORD_RE.match(f.name)\n        if not m or m.group(1) != stage:\n            continue\n        try:\n            attempts[int(m.group(2))] = _load_record(f, records_dir.name)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            continue\n    return attempts\n\n\ndef latest_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict | None:\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\n    return attempts[max(attempts)] if attempts else None\n\n\ndef next_attempt_number(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> int:\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\n    return (max(attempts) + 1) if attempts else 1\n\n\ndef latest_attempt_path(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> Path | None:\n    \"\"\"The path of the highest-numbered <stage>-NN.json, or None.\"\"\"\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\n    if not attempts:\n        return None\n    return records_dir / f\"{stage}-{max(attempts):02d}.json\"\n\n\ndef write_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str, record: dict, m: dict, item: str,\n                 log: str | None = None) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Every record gains record_version (this stage schema's own $id\n    version -- issue #60) and item (verbatim from the caller, matching the\n    record's directory segment), plus product_version (what ran, derived\n    here) and product_pin (what the tenant declared, copied verbatim from\n    the manifest, or null when the manifest carries no [attavo] table) --\n    the latter two recorded, never enforced (issue #49). A manifest\n    missing the table is an absent fact, not a crash: this is the one\n    caller of write_record that must not raise on a shape the manifest\n    schema forbids but tomllib.load happily returns.\n\n    Refuses (raises ValueError) a record carrying a key this stage's\n    schema does not declare -- the declared key set enforced with the\n    standard library, not a jsonschema import: bin/attavo is a single\n    script a tenant pins, and a runtime dependency changes installation.\n\n    Also refuses a `status: \"failed\"` record that carries no trail at all\n    -- log the empty or missing text it will sit beside, and refusal and\n    halted (where the stage's schema has them) both null (issue #53).\n    `returned`, `pass`, `halted`, and `refused` owe no such trail. log is\n    None for a stage that invoked no adapter (verify's `returned`), which\n    write_record then writes no log file for; otherwise the log is\n    written before the record, so a refusal leaves no half-pair.\"\"\"\n    records_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\n    schema = stage_schema(stage)\n    record = {**record, \"record_version\": schema_id_version(schema), \"item\": item,\n              \"product_version\": product_version(),\n              \"product_pin\": (m.get(\"attavo\") or {}).get(\"version\")}\n    undeclared = set(record) - set(schema.get(\"properties\", {}))\n    if undeclared:\n        raise ValueError(f\"write_record: {stage} record carries key(s) its schema does not \"\n                         f\"declare: {', '.join(sorted(undeclared))}\")\n    if (record.get(\"status\") == \"failed\" and not log\n            and record.get(\"refusal\") is None and record.get(\"halted\") is None):\n        raise ValueError(f\"write_record: {stage} record status is 'failed' with no log, \"\n                         f\"refusal, or halted to say why\")\n    path = records_dir / f\"{stage}-{nn:02d}.json\"\n    if log is not None:\n        path.with_suffix(\".log\").write_text(log)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n\n\n# --- stop: every non-pass build or verify record's class and cause (issue\n# #89) -- derived here, at write time, from the refusal, halted, and log\n# the caller already has. Never a fresh read of anything: the tenant zero\n# specimens this retires (#576 build-11, #659 build-01 and verify-01) are\n# exactly a stop the product wrote with nothing beside it to explain\n# itself after the fact. ---\n\nSTOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n               \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", \"question\",\n               \"environment\", \"gate\", \"died\", \"hung\")\nSTOP_PROVENANCES = (\"product\", \"tenant\", \"executor\", \"spec\")\n\n# Beyond the enum spelling itself, the prose issue #88 actually shipped\n# (adapters/claude-code/run and adapters/codex/run, on main since\n# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\n# it, in the transcript for the generic match below to find. Issue #94\n# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\n# (below): non-question's own halt line (\"halted: class non-question\")\n# would otherwise still satisfy the bare-name match here with no adapter\n# report-line field involved at all, and outlived-invocation's refusal\n# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\n# -- the same pattern issue #93 established for ceiling, just below,\n# rather than removed outright.\nCLASS_TEXT_MARKERS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n    \"non-question\": (),\n    \"outlived-invocation\": (),\n    # Issue #93: ceiling's own text-based check is CEILING_MARKERS, below,\n    # with provenance \"product\" -- a fact about the tool, not an executor\n    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\n    # default (the class's own name, \"ceiling\"), the generic match above\n    # would instead catch adapters/codex/run's and\n    # adapters/claude-code/run's own pre-emptive refusal -- which must\n    # carry the word \"ceiling\" by the same issue's own brief -- as\n    # provenance \"executor\", before CEILING_MARKERS is ever consulted.\n    \"ceiling\": (),\n    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\n    # -- status \"halted\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\n    # scanning for the literal word \"question\", which the question's own\n    # text very often contains regardless of what it is actually asking.\n    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\n    # question that happens to use the word \"question\" as executor\n    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\n    \"question\": (),\n    # environment/tenant (issue #115) is set directly by cmd_build's own\n    # preflight -- the one caller who knows a [checks].command exited 2\n    # on the approved tree -- never derived from adapter text. Left at\n    # the default, the generic match above would catch the word\n    # \"environment\" anywhere in a log or refusal (e.g. codex's own\n    # OPENAI_API_KEY auth-mismatch refusal, adapters/codex/run's\n    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\n    \"environment\": (),\n}\n\n# Known tool error text for a declared ceiling -- issue #86's own specimen\n# (codex's \"Input exceeds...\" line on a diff too large to judge) is\n# \"input_too_large\"; a matching line anywhere in the log, not only its\n# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \"[adapter exited\n# N]\" after whatever the tool itself printed. \"ceiling exceeded\" is issue\n# #93's own addition: both adapters now refuse pre-emptively, before the\n# tool is ever invoked, against a declared or fixed input limit, and\n# their refusal text is not caught by any of the three markers above.\nCEILING_MARKERS = (\"input_too_large\", \"exceeds the maximum context length\",\n                  \"context_length_exceeded\", \"ceiling exceeded\")\n\n\n# Issue #100's followups: an unclassed detail is the log's last line\n# verbatim, and that line is sometimes an adapter's own event JSON or a\n# tool's full error text -- thousands of characters wide. Capped here,\n# at write time, so a filed issue's own summary of it (file-stops'\n# log_tail already carries the full picture) stays short; the class\n# itself, \"unclassed\", already says the full explanation lives in the\n# log, not in this field.\nUNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS = 200\n\n\ndef _log_last_line(log: str | None) -> str:\n    lines = [l for l in (log or \"\").splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    last = lines[-1] if lines else \"\"\n    return last[:UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS]\n\n\ndef _carries_a_known_class(text: str | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\n    one of CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS' real-world phrasings of it, when that\n    class is not disabled there -- or None. Issue #88 is where an\n    adapter's own halt or refusal first named its class this way; issue\n    #93 added ceiling's own pre-emptive refusal to that set and disabled\n    its bare-name match (CEILING_MARKERS covers it instead); issue #94\n    disables non-question and outlived-invocation the same way, reading\n    both from the adapter's own report line (derive_stop's report_class)\n    now instead.\"\"\"\n    text = text or \"\"\n    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\n        markers = CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS.get(name, (name,))\n        if any(marker in text for marker in markers):\n            return name\n    return None\n\n\ndef derive_stop(status: str, *, refusal: str | None = None, halted: dict | None = None,\n                log: str | None = None, report_class: str | None = None,\n                refusal_provenance: str | None = None) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \"pass\",\n    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\n\n      - report_class -- payload.get(\"class\") off the adapter's own report\n        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\n        that class, provenance \"executor\". build.schema.json and\n        verify.schema.json stay untouched by issue #88 on purpose, so the\n        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\n        cmd_build or cmd_verify forwards on its own account; the caller\n        reads payload itself and passes this in, since only it still has\n        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\n        outlived-invocation's only path to a record now (issue #94):\n        CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS disables both for the text scan below, the\n        same way issue #93 disabled ceiling's bare-name match there. A\n        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\n        outlived-invocation today, since that refusal path prints no\n        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\n        other unnamed cause, until the adapter that raises it puts a\n        class on the line the way non-question already does.\n      - a halt carrying a non-empty halted.question, once it is not a\n        non-question caught above, is a genuine question -- question/spec,\n        with the question's own first line as detail (issue #100's\n        followups). This is the specimen issue #100 itself was built to\n        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\n        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\n        provenance -- a question is about the definition of done, which is\n        a person's or a ruling's to answer, never the product's own\n        mechanism.\n      - failing that, a refusal or the log itself that already names its\n        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\n        refusal) is that class, provenance \"executor\" -- the log is\n        checked because neither adapter's refusal *field* carries the\n        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\n        only the transcript\n      - a refusal that is not that -- the write-outside-claims path\n        itself, not the \"commit ... not authored by the executor\" shape\n        -- is claims-boundary/spec, unless the caller already knows this\n        refusal touched paths.records or paths.specs (issue #140:\n        protected_path_touched, checked ahead of the ordinary claims\n        match in cmd_build) and passes refusal_provenance=\"executor\" --\n        the product's own directories are not a claim a spec makes, so a\n        refusal there is not the spec's boundary to answer for\n      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\n        forge-unconcluded/tenant\n      - an adapter exit whose log carries a declared-ceiling error line is\n        ceiling/product\n      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\n        (capped at UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS) as its detail -- the other\n        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\n        evidence already lives in refusal, halted, forge_checks, or the\n        log itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if status == \"pass\":\n        return None\n    if status == \"returned\":\n        return {\"class\": \"forge-unconcluded\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": None}\n    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n        return {\"class\": report_class, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    question = (halted or {}).get(\"question\")\n    if status == \"halted\" and question:\n        return {\"class\": \"question\", \"provenance\": \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": question.splitlines()[0]}\n    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\n    if known:\n        return {\"class\": known, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    if status == \"refused\" and refusal is not None and not refusal.startswith(\"commit \"):\n        return {\"class\": \"claims-boundary\", \"provenance\": refusal_provenance or \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": None}\n    if log and any(marker in log.lower() for marker in CEILING_MARKERS):\n        return {\"class\": \"ceiling\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": None}\n    return {\"class\": \"unclassed\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": _log_last_line(log)}\n\n\ndef gate_stop(refusal: str | None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The stop for a refused spec-gate record: class \"gate\", provenance\n    \"spec\", the refusal string itself as cause (issue #137) -- not\n    derive_stop's generic claims-boundary/spec fallback issue #133\n    reused, which named a boundary the record never crossed: \"criterion\n    fails against the tree plus stub: doctor-template-absent.sh\" is not\n    a write outside claims. cmd_spec_gate is untouched by this lane, so\n    a spec record still carries no stop field of its own; this is\n    synthesized wherever a refused one is read (item_stops,\n    cmd_file_stops, proof_no_stop_lacks_cause), never persisted.\"\"\"\n    return {\"class\": \"gate\", \"provenance\": \"spec\", \"detail\": refusal}\n\n\ndef load_records(records_dir: Path) -> dict[str, dict[str, dict]]:\n    \"\"\"{item_id: {stage: latest_record}} for every <records>/<item>/<stage>-NN.json.\"\"\"\n    items: dict[str, dict[str, dict]] = {}\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return items\n    for item_dir in sorted(p for p in records_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir()):\n        by_stage: dict[str, dict[int, dict]] = {}\n        for rec in sorted(item_dir.glob(\"*.json\")):\n            m = RECORD_RE.match(rec.name)\n            if not m:\n                continue\n            stage, n = m.group(1), int(m.group(2))\n            try:\n                data = _load_record(rec, item_dir.name)\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                continue\n            by_stage.setdefault(stage, {})[n] = data\n        items[item_dir.name] = {stage: attempts[max(attempts)] for stage, attempts in by_stage.items()}\n    return items\n\n\n# --- doctor's three proofs ---\n\ndef proof_every_gate_rejects(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"every-gate-rejects\", \"every gate rejects its fixture\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no gate is registered\")\n    gates = m.get(\"gates\") or {}\n    if not gates:\n        return p.fail(\"[gates] is empty; a gate that has rejected nothing does not exist\")\n    fixtures = root / m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"rejections\", \"\")\n    # Proposal, not yet ruled on (issue #54): a gate that retires nothing\n    # only adds, so proof one reports it here rather than waiting on the\n    # schema alone -- read_manifest never validates against the manifest\n    # schema at runtime, so a schema requirement is not an enforced one.\n    no_retires = [name for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()) if not gate.get(\"retires\")]\n    missing, accepted = [], []\n    for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()):\n        fixture = fixtures / name\n        if not fixture.is_dir():\n            missing.append(name)\n            continue\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        item = fixture_item_id(fixture)\n        if item is not None:\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ITEM\"] = item\n        run = subprocess.run(gate[\"command\"], shell=True, cwd=str(fixture),\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\n        if run.returncode == 0:\n            accepted.append(name)\n    if missing:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no rejection fixture: {', '.join(missing)}\")\n    if accepted:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) that accepted their rejection fixture: {', '.join(accepted)}\")\n    if no_retires:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no retires: {', '.join(no_retires)}\")\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(gates)} gate(s) rejected their fixture\")\n\n\ndef merge_introducing_records(root: Path, records_rel: str, item: str,\n                              stages: tuple[str, ...]) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The merge commit reachable from HEAD whose first-parent diff\n    introduces a record for every one of stages, under\n    records_rel/item/ -- the same derivation attest itself uses\n    (derive_attest_items), read here so proof two requires an item's\n    stage records to have arrived by an actual merge, not merely to sit\n    in the tree (issue #69, acceptance row 4).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        merges = git(root, \"log\", \"--merges\", \"--format=%H\", \"HEAD\").split()\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return None\n    prefix = f\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item}/\"\n    for sha in merges:\n        try:\n            diff = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", f\"{sha}^1\", sha).splitlines()\n        except RuntimeError:\n            continue\n        found: set[str] = set()\n        for p in diff:\n            if p.startswith(prefix):\n                m = RECORD_RE.match(Path(p).name)\n                if m:\n                    found.add(m.group(1))\n        if all(s in found for s in stages):\n            return sha\n    return None\n\n\n# --- the invocation marker: the fact that a build or verify began, written\n# and committed before the adapter runs, so that an invocation which dies\n# or hangs before writing its own record is a fact on the branch (proof\n# five) rather than a silence (issue #151). ---\n\nINVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX = \".started\"\n\n\ndef invocation_marker_path(records_dir: Path, stage: str, nn: int) -> Path:\n    return records_dir / f\"{stage}-{nn:02d}{INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX}\"\n\n\ndef write_invocation_marker(root: Path, records_dir: Path, stage: str, nn: int) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The fact that an invocation began, written before it does: at,\n    host, pid, the sha it starts on, and the product that started it.\n    Its record's arrival is what retires it; a marker with no record is\n    an invocation that died or hangs, and proof five names it.\"\"\"\n    import os\n    import socket\n    records_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path = invocation_marker_path(records_dir, stage, nn)\n    sha = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    info = {\"at\": now_iso(), \"host\": socket.gethostname(), \"pid\": os.getpid(), \"sha\": sha,\n            \"product_version\": product_version()}\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(info, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n\n\ndef invocation_alive(info: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether the marker's pid is a live process on this host. Another\n    host's pid is unknowable from here and reads as not alive: a drive\n    that ran elsewhere and wrote no record is died by absence.\"\"\"\n    import os\n    import socket\n    if info.get(\"host\") != socket.gethostname():\n        return False\n    pid = info.get(\"pid\")\n    if not isinstance(pid, int) or isinstance(pid, bool) or pid <= 0:\n        return False\n    try:\n        os.kill(pid, 0)\n    except ProcessLookupError:\n        return False\n    except PermissionError:\n        return True\n    return True\n\n\ndef invocations_without_record(item_records_dir: Path) -> list[tuple[Path, dict]]:\n    \"\"\"Every <stage>-NN.started under one item whose <stage>-NN.json has\n    not arrived, with the marker's own dict ({} when unreadable).\"\"\"\n    out: list[tuple[Path, dict]] = []\n    if not item_records_dir.is_dir():\n        return out\n    for marker in sorted(item_records_dir.glob(f\"*{INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX}\")):\n        if (item_records_dir / f\"{marker.stem}.json\").is_file():\n            continue\n        try:\n            with marker.open() as fh:\n                info = json.load(fh)\n        except (OSError, ValueError):\n            info = {}\n        out.append((marker, info if isinstance(info, dict) else {}))\n    return out\n\n\ndef stall_bound_s(m: dict) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"[drive].stall_after_s: the tenant's own bound past which a live\n    invocation with no new event is hung. A bound the tenant did not\n    write is a forecast, so there is no default.\"\"\"\n    bound = (m.get(\"drive\") or {}).get(\"stall_after_s\")\n    if isinstance(bound, bool) or not isinstance(bound, (int, float)) or bound <= 0:\n        return None\n    return int(bound)\n\n\ndef proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"no-invocation-lacks-record\", \"no invocation lacks its record\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return p.fail(f\"no records directory under {records_dir}\")\n    if stall_bound_s(m) is None:\n        return p.fail(\"no [drive].stall_after_s in the manifest; a hung invocation cannot be \"\n                      \"told from a running one\")\n    recorded = 0\n    running: list[str] = []\n    problems: list[str] = []\n    for item_dir in sorted(d for d in records_dir.iterdir() if d.is_dir()):\n        for marker in item_dir.glob(f\"*{INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX}\"):\n            if (item_dir / f\"{marker.stem}.json\").is_file():\n                recorded += 1\n        for marker, info in invocations_without_record(item_dir):\n            name = f\"item {item_dir.name} {marker.stem}\"\n            if invocation_alive(info):\n                running.append(f\"{name} (pid {info.get('pid')} since {info.get('at')})\")\n                continue\n            problems.append(f\"{name} started {info.get('at')} on {info.get('host')} \"\n                            f\"pid {info.get('pid')} and never wrote its record\")\n    if problems:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(problems), unrecorded_invocations=len(problems),\n                      running_invocations=running)\n    return p.hold(f\"{recorded} invocation(s) recorded, {len(running)} running\",\n                  unrecorded_invocations=0, running_invocations=running)\n\n\ndef _events_path_for(root: Path, stage: str, nn: int) -> Path | None:\n    \"\"\"The adapter's own events file for this invocation, under the\n    checkout's git dir (a worktree's own dir when the checkout is one).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        gitdir = Path(git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-dir\").strip())\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return None\n    if not gitdir.is_absolute():\n        gitdir = root / gitdir\n    path = gitdir / \"attavo\" / f\"{stage}-{nn:02d}.events.jsonl\"\n    return path if path.is_file() else None\n\n\ndef _events_tail(path: Path | None, lines: int = 20) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The last lines of the adapter's own events file, as text for the\n    recovered record's own log -- or a line saying why there is none.\"\"\"\n    if path is None:\n        return \"no events file for this invocation\\n\"\n    try:\n        text = path.read_text()\n    except OSError:\n        return \"events file unreadable\\n\"\n    tail = text.splitlines()[-lines:]\n    return \"\\n\".join(tail) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef _seconds_since(at: str | None) -> float | None:\n    if not at:\n        return None\n    try:\n        then = datetime.strptime(at, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    except ValueError:\n        return None\n    return (datetime.now(timezone.utc) - then).total_seconds()\n\n\ndef _seconds_since_last_event(events_path: Path | None, started_at: str | None) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"How long since this invocation last wrote to its events file --\n    the file's own mtime, which is exactly when a new event last reached\n    disk, without reparsing every event line's own timestamp. Falls back\n    to the marker's own start time when there is no events file at all.\"\"\"\n    if events_path is not None:\n        return time.time() - events_path.stat().st_mtime\n    return _seconds_since(started_at)\n\n\ndef _drive_recover(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"`attavo drive --recover [N]`: every invocation of item N that began\n    and wrote no record ends in one here -- class died when its pid is\n    gone or on another host, class hung when it is alive past\n    [drive].stall_after_s with no newer event (and terminated); provenance\n    product; the events tail as the log. A live invocation inside the\n    bound is running and left alone. The record is committed and pushed\n    the way every stage record is; the ordinary relaunch then reads a\n    non-pass record and does what it does.\"\"\"\n    import os\n    import signal\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    bound = stall_bound_s(m)\n    if bound is None:\n        print(\"attavo drive: refused: no [drive].stall_after_s in the manifest; a hung \"\n              \"invocation cannot be told from a running one\")\n        return 1\n    pending = invocations_without_record(records_dir)\n    if not pending:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id}: every invocation has its record; nothing to recover\")\n        return 0\n    branch = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    try:\n        git(root, \"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\")\n        has_origin = True\n    except RuntimeError:\n        has_origin = False\n    recovered = 0\n    for marker, info in pending:\n        stage, nn_text = marker.stem.rsplit(\"-\", 1)\n        nn = int(nn_text)\n        events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)\n        log, last_at = _events_tail(events)\n        age = _seconds_since(last_at or info.get(\"at\"))\n        pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")\n        if invocation_alive(info):\n            if age is None or age <= bound:\n                print(f\"attavo drive: {marker.stem} is running (pid {pid}, last event \"\n                      f\"{'unknown' if age is None else int(age)} s ago, bound {bound} s); \"\n                      f\"nothing to recover\")\n                continue\n            cls = \"hung\"\n            try:\n                os.kill(int(pid), signal.SIGTERM)\n                ended = \"terminated\"\n            except OSError as exc:\n                ended = f\"not terminated ({exc})\"\n            detail = (f\"pid {pid} on {host} alive with no event for {int(age)} s \"\n                      f\"(bound {bound} s); {ended}\")\n        else:\n            cls = \"died\"\n            detail = (f\"pid {pid} on {host} is not running and wrote no {marker.stem}.json; \"\n                      f\"started {info.get('at')}, last event {last_at or 'none'}\")\n        if next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage) != nn:\n            print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {marker.name} names attempt {nn} but the next \"\n                  f\"{stage} record would be {next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage):02d}; \"\n                  f\"a later record already exists, read the records before recovering\")\n            return 1\n        schema = stage_schema(stage)\n        record = {k: None for k in schema.get(\"required\", [])}\n        approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\") or {}\n        record.update({\"sha\": info.get(\"sha\"), \"start_sha\": info.get(\"sha\"),\n                       \"approval_sha\": approval.get(\"sha\"), \"at\": info.get(\"at\"),\n                       \"adapter\": (m.get(\"executor\") or {}).get(stage),\n                       \"status\": \"failed\", \"refusal\": None, \"halted\": None,\n                       \"stop\": {\"class\": cls, \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": detail}})\n        if \"wall_clock_s\" in record:\n            record[\"wall_clock_s\"] = None if age is None else int(age)\n        record = {k: v for k, v in record.items() if k in schema.get(\"properties\", {})}\n        try:\n            path = write_record(records_dir, stage, record, m, item_id, log=log)\n        except ValueError as exc:\n            print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not write the {cls} record for {marker.stem}: {exc}\")\n            return 1\n        try:\n            commit_record(root, [path], f\"attavo: {stage} record for item {item_id} \"\n                                        f\"({path.stem}), recovered as {cls}\")\n        except RuntimeError as exc:\n            print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {cls} record: {exc}\")\n            return 1\n        if has_origin:\n            ok, err = push_record_commit(root, branch)\n            if not ok:\n                print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not push the {cls} record: {err}\")\n                return 1\n        else:\n            print(f\"attavo drive: note: no origin remote; {path.name} is committed, not pushed\")\n        print(f\"attavo drive: recovered {marker.stem} as {cls}: {detail}\")\n        recovered += 1\n    print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id}: {recovered} invocation(s) recovered\")\n    return 0\n\n\ndef proof_one_item_every_stage(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"one-item-every-stage\", \"one item has traversed every stage\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    items = load_records(records_dir)\n    if not items:\n        return p.fail(f\"no work item under {records_dir.relative_to(root)}\")\n    complete = [item for item, stages in items.items() if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\n    if not complete:\n        best = max(items.items(), key=lambda kv: len(kv[1]))\n        lacking = [s for s in STAGES if s not in best[1]]\n        return p.fail(f\"no item carries every stage; item {best[0]} lacks {', '.join(lacking)}\")\n\n    # issue #74: a complete item is counted only when its chain holds --\n    # attavo attest refuses a build re-approved after the fact or a\n    # verify whose build went stale, and the coherence gate refuses the\n    # merge group on exactly that; a proof that never asked would call a\n    # traversal the gate itself would not let through. The refusal text\n    # is check_attest_chain's own, never re-typed here.\n    refused, held, unmerged = [], [], []\n    for item in complete:\n        chain, message = check_attest_chain(records_dir / item, item)\n        if chain is None:\n            refused.append(f\"item {item}: {message}\")\n            continue\n        merge_sha = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES)\n        if merge_sha:\n            held.append((item, merge_sha))\n        else:\n            unmerged.append(item)\n\n    if held:\n        names = \", \".join(item for item, _ in held)\n        shas = \", \".join(sha[:12] for _, sha in held)\n        return p.hold(f\"item(s) {names} carry {', '.join(STAGES)} with the chain held, \"\n                      f\"merged at {shas}\")\n    if refused:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(refused))\n    return p.fail(f\"item(s) {', '.join(unmerged)} carry every stage with the chain held but no \"\n                  f\"merge commit's first-parent diff introduces all of them\")\n\n\ndef commit_subject(root: Path, sha: str) -> str:\n    return git(root, \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%s\", sha).strip()\n\n\ndef touches_boundary(root: Path, sha: str, boundary_paths: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether sha's first-parent diff touches a path [spec.boundary].paths\n    declares governed -- an ordinary merge that does is a boundary\n    evasion (issue #72): the tenant carried a governed change around the\n    path the manifest itself names.\"\"\"\n    diff = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", f\"{sha}^1\", sha).splitlines()\n    return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for path in diff for pattern in boundary_paths)\n\n\ndef proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"no-commit-lacks-record\", \"no commit lacks a record\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; the tenant has no record boundary\")\n    try:\n        install = git(root, \"log\", \"--diff-filter=A\", \"--format=%H\",\n                      \"--reverse\", \"--\", MANIFEST).split()\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        return p.fail(f\"git: {exc}\")\n    if not install:\n        return p.fail(f\"{MANIFEST} is not committed; the tenant has no record boundary\")\n    install_sha = install[0]\n    full_chain = git(root, \"rev-list\", f\"{install_sha}..HEAD\", \"--first-parent\").split()\n    if not full_chain:\n        return p.fail(f\"no commit after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}; nothing has been recorded\")\n\n    # issue #74: [doctor] from lets a tenant declare the doctor's read to\n    # start at a later commit on main's first-parent line -- the point\n    # after which every push arrived through the queue -- rather than the\n    # install commit, which on a repository that adopted the product\n    # after its history began is a boundary the doctor cannot otherwise\n    # see. Any spelling git resolves is accepted (a short sha, a tag, a\n    # ref) -- resolved with rev-parse --verify before the first-parent\n    # check runs, so the two failure modes stay distinct: a spelling that\n    # names no commit at all, and a commit that names one off the line.\n    # Checked, not trusted: neither is silently forgiven back to install.\n    declared_from = (m.get(\"doctor\") or {}).get(\"from\")\n    window_start = install_sha\n    if declared_from is not None:\n        try:\n            resolved_from = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", f\"{declared_from}^{{commit}}\").strip()\n        except RuntimeError:\n            return p.fail(f\"[doctor] from {declared_from} does not resolve to a commit\")\n        if resolved_from != install_sha and resolved_from not in full_chain:\n            return p.fail(f\"[doctor] from {declared_from} is not on main's first-parent \"\n                          f\"line after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}\")\n        window_start = resolved_from\n\n    if window_start == install_sha:\n        window_spec = f\"{install_sha}..HEAD\"\n        commits = full_chain\n    else:\n        window_spec = f\"{window_start}^..HEAD\"\n        commits = git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\").split()\n    before_window = len(full_chain) - len(commits)\n\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    named: set[str] = set()\n    for stages in load_records(records_dir).values():\n        for rec in stages.values():\n            sha = rec.get(\"sha\")\n            if isinstance(sha, str):\n                named.add(sha)\n            for c in rec.get(\"commits\", []) or []:\n                if isinstance(c, str):\n                    named.add(c)\n    record_commits = set(git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\",\n                             \"--\", records_rel).split()) if records_rel else set()\n    merges = set(git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\", \"--merges\").split())\n    boundary_paths = ((m.get(\"spec\") or {}).get(\"boundary\") or {}).get(\"paths\") or []\n\n    # Every first-parent commit in the window is exactly one of three\n    # (issue #72): recorded (a record names it, or its diff touches\n    # paths.records), ordinary (a merge that doesn't), or unrecorded\n    # (anything else -- on a protected main with a queue, a non-merge\n    # commit is the only way a change arrives without the forge).\n    recorded, ordinary, unrecorded = [], [], []\n    ordinary_commits, unrecorded_commits = [], []\n    boundary_evasions = 0\n    for c in commits:\n        if c in named or c in record_commits:\n            recorded.append(c)\n        elif c in merges:\n            ordinary.append(c)\n            evasion = bool(boundary_paths and touches_boundary(root, c, boundary_paths))\n            if evasion:\n                boundary_evasions += 1\n            ordinary_commits.append({\"sha\": c, \"subject\": commit_subject(root, c),\n                                     \"boundary_evasion\": evasion})\n        else:\n            unrecorded.append(c)\n            unrecorded_commits.append({\"sha\": c, \"subject\": commit_subject(root, c)})\n\n    counts = f\"{len(recorded)} recorded, {len(ordinary)} ordinary, {len(unrecorded)} unrecorded\"\n    evasions = boundary_evasions if boundary_paths else \"n/a\"\n    extra = {\"recorded\": len(recorded), \"ordinary\": len(ordinary),\n             \"unrecorded\": len(unrecorded), \"boundary_evasions\": evasions,\n             \"before_window\": before_window,\n             \"ordinary_commits\": ordinary_commits, \"unrecorded_commits\": unrecorded_commits}\n    if unrecorded:\n        return p.fail(f\"{unrecorded[-1][:12]} lacks a record; {counts}; boundary evasions: \"\n                      f\"{evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\", **extra)\n    return p.hold(f\"{counts}; boundary evasions: {evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\",\n                  **extra)\n\n\nADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\[adapter exited \\d+\\]$\")\n\n\ndef _log_owes_tool_error(log: str | None) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True when a log's last non-empty line is exactly an adapter-exit\n    marker and every line before it parses as JSON -- an adapter's own\n    event stream, never a tool's own words (issue #94's own specimen,\n    tenant zero's attest/records/659/verify-01.log: codex's\n    \"thread.started\" event, then nothing but \"[adapter exited 1]\" -- the\n    tool's real error line dropped before this reached the log, issue\n    #86's own bug in split_adapter_stdout). A log that is only the exit\n    marker, nothing before it at all, still owes the same line.\"\"\"\n    if not log:\n        return False\n    lines = [l for l in log.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    if not lines or not ADAPTER_EXIT_RE.match(lines[-1]):\n        return False\n    for l in lines[:-1]:\n        try:\n            json.loads(l)\n        except ValueError:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"no-stop-lacks-cause\", \"no stop lacks its cause\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return p.fail(f\"no records directory under {records_dir}\")\n\n    # issue #89's own window lesson, proof three's already: a record\n    # before record_version 3 has no stop by construction (schema\n    # versions 1 and 2 predate it) -- counted here, never refused.\n    older = 0\n    checked = 0\n    problems: list[str] = []\n    for item_dir in sorted(d for d in records_dir.iterdir() if d.is_dir()):\n        for stage in STOP_STAGES:\n            for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, stage).items()):\n                if rec.get(\"record_version\", 1) < 3:\n                    older += 1\n                    continue\n                if rec.get(\"status\") == \"pass\":\n                    continue\n                checked += 1\n                name = f\"{stage}-{n:02d}\"\n                stop = rec.get(\"stop\")\n                if not stop:\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} carries no stop\")\n                    continue\n                cls, provenance = stop.get(\"class\"), stop.get(\"provenance\")\n                if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \"\n                                    f\"no enumerated class\")\n                    continue\n                if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \"\n                                    f\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\")\n                    continue\n                if cls == \"unclassed\" and not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is unclassed with no detail\")\n                    continue\n                log_path = item_dir / f\"{name}.log\"\n                log = log_path.read_text() if log_path.is_file() else None\n                # Issue #89, rejection test 1's own specimen (tenant\n                # zero's #659 build-01): a failed build that actually ran\n                # the gates -- selected_tests is set only once cmd_build\n                # reaches them -- owes their heading in the log, whatever\n                # else stop already says.\n                if (stage == \"build\" and rec.get(\"status\") == \"failed\"\n                        and rec.get(\"selected_tests\") is not None\n                        and \"--- attavo gates, iteration\" not in (log or \"\")):\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} failed after the gates ran \"\n                                    f\"but its log carries no gates heading\")\n                    continue\n                if _log_owes_tool_error(log):\n                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name}'s log ends in an adapter \"\n                                    f\"exit with nothing before it but event lines; the tool's \"\n                                    f\"own error line is owed\")\n\n        # issue #137: a refused spec-gate record is a stop too, class\n        # \"gate\" -- synthesized the same way item_stops and\n        # cmd_file_stops already read it, since cmd_spec_gate itself\n        # carries no stop field to check for one. No record_version\n        # gate here: unlike build/verify's own stop field, gate is never\n        # persisted, so there is no older shape that predates it.\n        for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, \"spec\").items()):\n            if rec.get(\"status\") != \"refused\":\n                continue\n            checked += 1\n            name = f\"spec-{n:02d}\"\n            stop = gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\"))\n            cls, provenance = stop[\"class\"], stop[\"provenance\"]\n            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \"\n                                f\"no enumerated class\")\n                continue\n            if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \"\n                                f\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\")\n                continue\n            if not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is a gate stop with no cause\")\n\n    older_note = f\"{older} record(s) before stop was recorded\"\n    if problems:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(problems), older_records=older)\n    return p.hold(f\"{checked} checked ({older_note})\" if checked == 0\n                 else f\"{checked} non-pass record(s) carry stop with a cause ({older_note})\",\n                 older_records=older)\n\n\ndef doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\n            proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\n            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\n            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m),\n            proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root, m)]\n\n\ndef cmd_doctor(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n    args = [a for a in argv if a != \"--json\"]\n    root = Path(args[0] if args else \".\").resolve()\n    proofs = doctor(root)\n    if as_json:\n        print(json.dumps({\"root\": str(root), \"done\": all(p.holds for p in proofs),\n                          \"proofs\": [p.as_dict() for p in proofs]}, indent=2))\n    else:\n        for i, p in enumerate(proofs, 1):\n            print(f\"proof {i} {p.key}: {'HOLDS' if p.holds else 'FAILS'}: {p.reason}\")\n        print(\"doctor: done\" if all(p.holds for p in proofs)\n              else f\"doctor: not done ({sum(not p.holds for p in proofs)} of \"\n                   f\"{len(proofs)} proofs fail)\")\n    return 0 if all(p.holds for p in proofs) else 1\n\n\n# --- the spec contract ---\n\ndef parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict | None, str | None]:\n    lines = spec_md.read_text().splitlines()\n    heading_idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## \")]\n    headings = [lines[i].rstrip() for i in heading_idx]\n    expected = [\"## Problem\", \"## Claims\", \"## Criteria\"]\n    if headings != expected:\n        bad = next((h for h in headings if h not in expected), None)\n        if bad is None:\n            missing = [h for h in expected if h not in headings]\n            bad = missing[0] if missing else \"heading order\"\n        return None, f\"headings: found {headings or ['(none)']}, expected {expected} ({bad})\"\n    idx_problem, idx_claims, idx_criteria = heading_idx\n    claims = [l.strip()[2:].strip() for l in lines[idx_claims + 1:idx_criteria]\n              if l.strip().startswith(\"- \")]\n    criteria = []\n    for l in lines[idx_criteria + 1:]:\n        s = l.strip()\n        if not s.startswith(\"- \") or \":\" not in s:\n            continue\n        name = s[2:].split(\":\", 1)[0].strip()\n        criteria.append(name)\n    return {\"claims\": claims, \"criteria\": criteria}, None\n\n\ndef run_criterion(exe: Path, cwd: Path) -> int:\n    try:\n        run = subprocess.run([str(exe)], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True,\n                             timeout=CRITERION_TIMEOUT, check=False)\n        return run.returncode\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        return 124\n    except OSError:\n        return 126\n\n\ndef parse_removed(stub_dir: Path) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"The paths listed in stub/.removed, one per line, comments (lines\n    starting with #) and blank lines ignored. [] when the stub carries no\n    .removed at all.\n    \"\"\"\n    removed_file = stub_dir / \".removed\"\n    if not removed_file.is_file():\n        return []\n    paths = []\n    for line in removed_file.read_text().splitlines():\n        s = line.strip()\n        if not s or s.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        paths.append(s)\n    return paths\n\n\ndef removed_path_refusal(root: Path, stub_dir: Path, rel: str) -> str | None:\n    p = Path(rel)\n    if p.is_absolute() or \"..\" in p.parts:\n        return f\"stub/.removed names a path outside the tree: {rel}\"\n    if not (root / p).exists():\n        return f\"stub/.removed names a path not in the tree: {rel}\"\n    if (stub_dir / p).exists():\n        return f\"stub/.removed names a path the stub also supplies: {rel}\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef stub_removed_refusal(root: Path, spec_dir: Path) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Validated by name, before any criterion runs -- a stub whose\n    .removed cannot be applied has no meaning to gate against.\n    \"\"\"\n    stub_dir = spec_dir / \"stub\"\n    for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\n        refusal = removed_path_refusal(root, stub_dir, rel)\n        if refusal:\n            return refusal\n    return None\n\n\ndef run_criteria(root: Path, spec_dir: Path, names: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\n    criteria_dir = spec_dir / \"criteria\"\n    stub_dir = spec_dir / \"stub\"\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        tree = Path(tmp) / \"tree\"\n        stubbed = Path(tmp) / \"stubbed\"\n        shutil.copytree(root, tree, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\".git\"))\n        shutil.copytree(root, stubbed, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\".git\"))\n        if stub_dir.is_dir():\n            shutil.copytree(stub_dir, stubbed, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n            for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\n                target = stubbed / rel\n                if target.is_dir():\n                    shutil.rmtree(target)\n                elif target.exists():\n                    target.unlink()\n            removed_marker = stubbed / \".removed\"\n            if removed_marker.exists():\n                removed_marker.unlink()\n        results = []\n        for name in names:\n            exe = criteria_dir / name\n            results.append({\"name\": name,\n                            \"on_tree\": run_criterion(exe, tree),\n                            \"on_stub\": run_criterion(exe, stubbed)})\n        return results\n\n\ndef commit_postdates(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether later is a strict descendant of earlier on this branch.\"\"\"\n    if earlier == later:\n        return False\n    run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", earlier, later],\n                         capture_output=True, check=False)\n    return run.returncode == 0\n\n\ndef cmd_spec_gate(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo spec-gate: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo spec-gate: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    spec_md = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n    if not spec_md.is_file():\n        print(f\"attavo spec-gate: no spec at {spec_dir}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    spec_rel = str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id)\n    try:\n        spec_sha = last_commit_touching(root, spec_rel)\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo spec-gate: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    try:\n        approved = approval_status(root, m, item_id) == \"valid\"\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo spec-gate: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    latest_approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\")\n    if approved:\n        record = {\"sha\": git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip(), \"spec_sha\": spec_sha,\n                  \"at\": now_iso(), \"status\": \"approved\",\n                  \"approval_sha\": latest_approval.get(\"sha\") if latest_approval else None,\n                  \"criteria\": [], \"refusal\": None}\n        write_record(records_dir, \"spec\", record, m, item_id)\n        print(\"attavo spec-gate: approved (no criteria run)\")\n        return 0\n\n    # Third verdict, beside \"approved\" and Phase 1's \"pass\": the approval\n    # is not valid, but a build already ran after it -- the amendment that\n    # expired the approval landed above the line, not below it, and the\n    # tree the build produced is what must satisfy the criteria now, not\n    # the stub that only ever proved they were reachable before approval.\n    # Issue #98: whatever the build's status, including a halt -- the\n    # executor commits then asks, so a halted build's sha postdating the\n    # approval means it did the work. commit_postdates already excludes a\n    # halt that committed nothing, since such a build's sha equals its\n    # start_sha and so postdates nothing.\n    latest_build = latest_record(records_dir, \"build\")\n    built = bool(\n        latest_approval and latest_build\n        and commit_postdates(root, latest_approval[\"sha\"], latest_build[\"sha\"]))\n\n    parsed, refusal = parse_spec(spec_md)\n    results: list[dict] = []\n    if refusal is None:\n        if built:\n            refusal = stub_removed_refusal(root, spec_dir)\n            if refusal is None:\n                # Per criterion, not the set: passing on the tree is what\n                # the build already satisfied; failing on the tree but\n                # passing on the stub is a new obligation the next build\n                # must meet -- an operator scripting a ruling the executor\n                # skipped. Refused only when a criterion satisfies neither.\n                results = run_criteria(root, spec_dir, parsed[\"criteria\"])\n                fail = next((c for c in results if c[\"on_tree\"] != 0 and c[\"on_stub\"] != 0), None)\n                if fail:\n                    refusal = f\"criterion fails against the tree plus stub: {fail['name']}\"\n        elif not parsed[\"claims\"]:\n            refusal = \"claims: empty; the build may touch nothing\"\n        else:\n            criteria_dir = spec_dir / \"criteria\"\n            listed = parsed[\"criteria\"]\n            existing = sorted(p.name for p in criteria_dir.iterdir()) if criteria_dir.is_dir() else []\n            prose = None\n            for name in listed:\n                if name not in existing:\n                    prose = name\n                    break\n            if prose is None:\n                for name in existing:\n                    if name not in listed:\n                        prose = name\n                        break\n            if prose is None:\n                for name in listed:\n                    if not os.access(criteria_dir / name, os.X_OK):\n                        prose = name\n                        break\n            if prose:\n                refusal = f\"criterion is prose: {prose}\"\n            else:\n                refusal = stub_removed_refusal(root, spec_dir)\n                if refusal is None:\n                    results = run_criteria(root, spec_dir, listed)\n                    fail_tree = next((c for c in results if c[\"on_tree\"] == 0), None)\n                    if fail_tree:\n                        refusal = f\"criterion passes against the tree: {fail_tree['name']}\"\n                    else:\n                        fail_stub = next((c for c in results if c[\"on_stub\"] != 0), None)\n                        if fail_stub:\n                            refusal = f\"criterion fails against the tree plus stub: {fail_stub['name']}\"\n\n    status = \"refused\" if refusal else (\"built\" if built else \"pass\")\n    record = {\"sha\": git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip(),\n              \"spec_sha\": spec_sha,\n              \"at\": now_iso(), \"status\": status, \"approval_sha\": None,\n              \"criteria\": results, \"refusal\": refusal}\n    write_record(records_dir, \"spec\", record, m, item_id)\n\n    if refusal:\n        print(f\"attavo spec-gate: refused: {refusal}\")\n        return 1\n    print(f\"attavo spec-gate: {status} ({len(results)} criterion/criteria)\")\n    return 0\n\n\n# --- approval, bound to a commit ---\n\ndef cmd_approve(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    by = None\n    positional: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(argv):\n        if argv[i] == \"--by\":\n            by = argv[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(argv) else None\n            i += 2\n        else:\n            positional.append(argv[i])\n            i += 1\n    item_id = positional[0] if positional else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo approve: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    if not by:\n        print(\"attavo approve: --by LOGIN is required\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo approve: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    spec_rel = str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id)\n    try:\n        spec_sha_now = last_commit_touching(root, spec_rel)\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo approve: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    latest_spec = latest_record(records_dir, \"spec\")\n    approvers = ((m.get(\"operators\") or {}).get(\"approvers\")) or []\n\n    refusal = None\n    if latest_spec is None or latest_spec.get(\"status\") not in (\"pass\", \"built\"):\n        refusal = f\"no passing spec-gate record for item {item_id}\"\n    elif latest_spec.get(\"spec_sha\") != spec_sha_now:\n        refusal = (f\"spec-gate record is stale: recorded {latest_spec.get('spec_sha')}, \"\n                   f\"spec now at {spec_sha_now}\")\n    elif by not in approvers:\n        refusal = f\"{by} is not in [operators].approvers\"\n\n    if refusal:\n        print(f\"attavo approve: refused: {refusal}\")\n        return 1\n\n    record = {\"sha\": git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip(), \"spec_sha\": spec_sha_now,\n              \"approved_by\": by, \"at\": now_iso()}\n    write_record(records_dir, \"approval\", record, m, item_id)\n    print(f\"attavo approve: item {item_id} approved by {by}\")\n    return 0\n\n\ndef approval_status(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\"absent\", \"expired\", or \"valid\": whether the latest approval record\n    for item_id still binds to the spec's current commit. Raises\n    ShallowCheckoutError on a shallow checkout, same as last_commit_touching.\n    Shared by cmd_approval_status and cmd_build so build refuses on exactly\n    what `attavo approval-status` would print.\n    \"\"\"\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    spec_rel = str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id)\n    spec_sha_now = last_commit_touching(root, spec_rel)\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    latest_approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\")\n\n    if latest_approval is None:\n        return \"absent\"\n    if latest_approval.get(\"spec_sha\") == spec_sha_now:\n        return \"valid\"\n    return \"expired\"\n\n\ndef cmd_approval_status(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo approval-status: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo approval-status: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    try:\n        status = approval_status(root, m, item_id)\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo approval-status: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    print(status)\n    return 0 if status == \"valid\" else 1\n\n\n# --- build: adapter, claims boundary, criteria, and the tenant's tests ---\n\nSTAGE_NAMES = (\"build\", \"verify\", \"counsel\")\n\n\ndef merge_adapter_config(m: dict, adapter_name: str, stage: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"[executor.<adapter>] merged with [executor.<adapter>.<stage>], the\n    stage table shadowing the parent for that stage only. Both build and\n    verify call this before setting ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the\n    record's adapter_config is the merged result.\"\"\"\n    parent = (m.get(\"executor\") or {}).get(adapter_name) or {}\n    if not isinstance(parent, dict):\n        return {}\n    merged = {k: v for k, v in parent.items() if k not in STAGE_NAMES}\n    stage_table = parent.get(stage)\n    if isinstance(stage_table, dict):\n        merged.update(stage_table)\n    return merged\n\n\ndef resolve_adapter(root: Path, name: str) -> Path | None:\n    \"\"\"adapters/<name>/run, resolved first under the tenant's own\n    attavo/adapters/, then under this product's adapters/.\"\"\"\n    for base in (root / \"attavo\" / \"adapters\", PRODUCT_ROOT / \"adapters\"):\n        candidate = base / name / \"run\"\n        if candidate.is_file():\n            return candidate\n    return None\n\n\ndef adapter_reports(adapter_path: Path) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Field names adapters/<name>/conformance.json declares this adapter\n    can supply with a real value -- vendor independence (2026-09-09\n    ruling): the record carries the declaration, so an adapter claiming\n    a field and returning null for it fails the conformance suite\n    instead of writing a silent, uncomparable null. [] when the\n    resolved adapter (a tenant override included) declares no\n    conformance.json at all -- an absent declaration, not a refusal.\"\"\"\n    manifest_path = adapter_path.parent / \"conformance.json\"\n    if not manifest_path.is_file():\n        return []\n    try:\n        manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return []\n    return manifest.get(\"reports\", [])\n\n\ndef changed_paths(root: Path, start_sha: str, records_rel: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Paths changed between start_sha and HEAD, other than paths.records --\n    the records directory is where build itself writes, not a claim.\"\"\"\n    out = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", start_sha, \"HEAD\").splitlines()\n    prefix = records_rel.rstrip(\"/\") + \"/\"\n    return [p for p in out if p and p != records_rel and not p.startswith(prefix)]\n\n\ndef matches_a_claim(path: str, claims: list[str]) -> bool:\n    return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for pattern in claims)\n\n\ndef protected_path_touched(root: Path, start_sha: str, records_rel: str,\n                           specs_rel: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The first path an executor's own commits touched under\n    paths.records or paths.specs since start_sha, or None (issue #140).\n    Neither directory is a claim a spec can make -- paths.records is\n    where the product itself writes, paths.specs is the definition of\n    done -- yet changed_paths above excludes paths.records from the\n    ordinary claims check entirely, so a path there never even reached\n    matches_a_claim to be refused: tenant zero's own item #688 committed\n    its own events file this way, under its records directory, on a\n    build that then passed. Checked directly against the raw diff, not\n    changed_paths's already-filtered list.\"\"\"\n    touched = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", start_sha, \"HEAD\").splitlines()\n    protected = []\n    for rel in (records_rel, specs_rel):\n        stripped = rel.rstrip(\"/\")\n        protected.append((stripped, stripped + \"/\"))\n    for p in touched:\n        if not p:\n            continue\n        for exact, prefix in protected:\n            if p == exact or p.startswith(prefix):\n                return p\n    return None\n\n\ndef executor_identity(adapter_name: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The executor's identity (issue #33): set by the product, never the\n    tenant's git config, so an executor commit is never indistinguishable\n    from an operator's own -- the specimen is attavo/code-factory@e22fa85.\n    A reserved, undeliverable domain (.invalid) so no mailbox is implied.\n    Distinct from the records app identity: the app says the product\n    pushed this, this says an invocation authored this -- different\n    facts, neither borrows the other's name.\"\"\"\n    return {\"name\": f\"attavo executor ({adapter_name})\",\n            \"email\": f\"executor+{adapter_name}@attavo.invalid\"}\n\n\ndef driver_identity() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The driver's identity: set by the product, never the tenant's git\n    config, so a driver's own transport commit -- a record commit\n    `commit_record` makes on the driver's behalf -- is never\n    indistinguishable from an operator's own; `git log --author='attavo\n    driver'` on a driven item lists exactly those commits. Distinct from\n    executor_identity: that names an adapter invocation's own commits,\n    this names the transport that carries a stage's record.\"\"\"\n    return {\"name\": \"attavo driver\", \"email\": \"driver@attavo.invalid\"}\n\n\n# The stop classes issue #89 gave no code of their own beyond the guard\n# that raised them -- non-question and outlived-invocation from an\n# adapter's own pre-emptive refusal, forge-unconcluded from a returned\n# verify, ceiling from a declared-input-limit error, claims-boundary from\n# the write-outside-claims refusal, repeated-act from... the same shape,\n# environment from cmd_build's own [checks].command preflight (issue\n# #115). question (a person's to answer) and the residual (no-cause,\n# unclassed -- nobody has looked yet) are not in this tuple; attavo stops\n# (issue #129) is the one reader, so it lives beside driver_identity,\n# not beside derive_stop, which never needs to tell a guard from any\n# other class once it has already named one.\nGUARDED_STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"forge-unconcluded\", \"ceiling\",\n                        \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"environment\")\n\n\ndef stop_class_enum() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Every class a stop can name, read from the build record schema's own\n    enum (issue #129) rather than retyped -- STOP_CLASSES already drifted\n    once (environment arrived in the schema before anything but derive_stop\n    read it); a second copy is a second place to forget. build's schema is\n    read, not verify's: verify's own enum is a strict subset (it never\n    raises environment, cmd_build's own preflight alone).\"\"\"\n    schema = stage_schema(\"build\")\n    return tuple(schema[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"])\n\n\ndef commits_since(root: Path, start_sha: str, end: str = \"HEAD\") -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"(sha, name, email) for every commit after start_sha up to and\n    including end, first-parent only, oldest first. cmd_build's own call\n    (start_sha at the invocation, end left at the default HEAD) never sees\n    a merge in that window, so --first-parent changes nothing there;\n    issue #128's ledger is the caller that needs it, to walk one branch's\n    own line without a concurrent merge to main expanding into every\n    commit main gained meanwhile.\"\"\"\n    out = git(root, \"log\", \"--first-parent\", \"--reverse\",\n             \"--format=%H\\x1f%an\\x1f%ae\", f\"{start_sha}..{end}\")\n    commits = []\n    for line in out.splitlines():\n        if not line.strip():\n            continue\n        sha, name, email = line.split(\"\\x1f\")\n        commits.append({\"sha\": sha, \"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n    return commits\n\n\ndef split_adapter_stdout(stdout: str) -> tuple[str, dict | None]:\n    \"\"\"(transcript, payload): the adapter's last non-empty stdout line is\n    its JSON report, and everything before it is transcript, only when\n    that last line actually parses as JSON. When it does not -- a tool's\n    own error line printed last on a non-zero exit (issue #86: tenant\n    zero attest/records/659/verify-01.log, codex's own \"Input exceeds...\"\n    line, dropped because it was mistaken for an attempted payload) --\n    nothing here is a report, and the whole stdout is the transcript, so\n    that last line is not silently lost.\n    \"\"\"\n    lines = stdout.splitlines()\n    non_empty = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.strip()]\n    if not non_empty:\n        return stdout, None\n    last = non_empty[-1]\n    try:\n        payload = json.loads(lines[last])\n    except ValueError:\n        return stdout, None\n    transcript = \"\\n\".join(lines[:last])\n    return transcript, payload\n\n\n# --- events: the adapter contract's one optional output (issue #26) --\n# an uncommitted <stage>-NN.events.jsonl the screen tails while a stage\n# runs, never a record and never committed (commit_record names only\n# .json, .log, and .filed; this suffix is never among them). Written\n# under the checkout's own git directory, not the working tree (issue\n# #140): tenant zero's own item #688 committed its events file for\n# real -- the executor's own commit staged it, because it sat inside\n# the tree the executor runs `git status` against. ---\n\nEVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS = 400\n\n\ndef stage_events_dir(root: Path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"<git-dir>/attavo, absolute -- <checkout>/.git/attavo for an\n    ordinary checkout, <main-repo>/.git/worktrees/<name>/attavo for a\n    linked worktree (issue #140). Outside the working tree either way,\n    so a file written here never appears in `git status` in root and is\n    never at risk of being staged and committed by the executor; the\n    screen's seam finds it the same way, with the same command, in its\n    own worktree.\"\"\"\n    git_dir = Path(git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\").strip())\n    events_dir = git_dir / \"attavo\"\n    events_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    return events_dir\n\n\ndef append_event(events_path: Path, kind: str, text: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One {at, kind, text} JSON line appended to events_path and flushed\n    at once (open-write-close, not a kept handle) -- the screen tails\n    this file while the stage is still running, so a line held in a\n    buffer is a line the feed does not move on. text is collapsed to one\n    line and capped at EVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS: a tool result can be a whole\n    file, and the feed renders lines, not files.\"\"\"\n    line = {\"at\": now_iso(), \"kind\": kind,\n            \"text\": \" \".join(text.split())[:EVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS]}\n    with events_path.open(\"a\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(line) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef cmd_build(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo build: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo build: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    adapter_name = (m.get(\"executor\") or {}).get(\"build\")\n    if not adapter_name:\n        print(\"attavo build: refused: no [executor].build in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n\n    tests_cfg = m.get(\"tests\") or {}\n    if not tests_cfg.get(\"select\") or not tests_cfg.get(\"run\"):\n        print(\"attavo build: refused: no [tests] table in the manifest \"\n              \"([tests].select and [tests].run are both required)\")\n        return 1\n\n    try:\n        status = approval_status(root, m, item_id)\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo build: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    if status != \"valid\":\n        print(f\"attavo build: refused: approval is {status}\")\n        return 1\n\n    adapter_path = resolve_adapter(root, adapter_name)\n    if adapter_path is None:\n        print(f\"attavo build: refused: no adapter named {adapter_name!r}\")\n        return 1\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    spec_sha = last_commit_touching(root, str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id))\n    latest_approval = latest_record(item_records_dir, \"approval\")\n    parsed, _ = parse_spec(spec_dir / \"spec.md\")\n    claims = parsed[\"claims\"] if parsed else []\n    criteria_names = parsed[\"criteria\"] if parsed else []\n    adapter_config = merge_adapter_config(m, adapter_name, \"build\")\n    checks_command = (m.get(\"checks\") or {}).get(\"command\")\n    identity = executor_identity(adapter_name)\n    reports = adapter_reports(adapter_path)\n\n    start_sha = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    branch = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    started = time.monotonic()\n\n    # Issue #115: the tenant's whole-tree checks run once here, on the\n    # approved tree, before the adapter is ever invoked -- exit 2 means\n    # the command itself cannot run (e.g. a missing import at test\n    # collection, item #106's build-01), not a failing check, and no\n    # build could have passed against it. Exit 0 or 1 -- the checks run\n    # and pass or fail, the expected states before a build -- proceeds;\n    # the per-iteration checks below run (and are recorded) exactly as\n    # before.\n    if checks_command:\n        preflight = subprocess.run(checks_command, shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                   capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n        if preflight.returncode == 2:\n            detail = _log_last_line(preflight.stdout + \"\\n\" + preflight.stderr)\n            record = {\n                \"sha\": start_sha,\n                \"start_sha\": start_sha,\n                \"spec_sha\": spec_sha,\n                \"approval_sha\": latest_approval.get(\"sha\") if latest_approval else None,\n                \"at\": now_iso(),\n                \"adapter\": adapter_name,\n                \"adapter_config\": adapter_config,\n                \"executor_identity\": identity,\n                \"reports\": reports,\n                \"adapter_version\": None,\n                \"model\": None,\n                \"model_version\": None,\n                \"iterations\": 1,\n                \"criteria\": [],\n                \"selected_tests\": None,\n                \"checks\": {\"command\": checks_command, \"exit\": preflight.returncode},\n                \"tokens\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0},\n                \"cost_usd\": None,\n                \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n                \"status\": \"refused\",\n                \"refusal\": \"[checks].command exited 2 on the approved tree\",\n                \"halted\": None,\n                \"stop\": {\"class\": \"environment\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": detail},\n            }\n            record_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"build\", record, m, item_id,\n                                       log=preflight.stdout + preflight.stderr)\n            print(f\"attavo build: refused ({record_path.name})\")\n            return 1\n\n    adapter_version = model = model_version = None\n    tokens = {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0}\n    cost_usd = None\n    transcripts: list[str] = []\n    criteria_results: list[dict] = []\n    selected_tests: dict | None = None\n    checks_result: dict | None = None\n    status_out = \"failed\"\n    refusal = None\n    refusal_provenance = None\n    halted = None\n    iterations_used = 0\n\n    events_path = stage_events_dir(root) / f\"build-{next_attempt_number(item_records_dir, 'build'):02d}.events.jsonl\"\n\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        feedback_path = Path(tmp) / \"feedback.txt\"\n        feedback_path.write_text(\"\")\n\n        for iteration in range(1, BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET + 1):\n            iterations_used = iteration\n            append_event(events_path, \"iteration\", f\"iteration {iteration} of {BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET}\")\n            env = dict(os.environ)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"] = str(spec_dir)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR\"] = str(item_records_dir)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\"] = str(root / m[\"paths\"][\"rulings\"])\n            env[\"ATTAVO_BRANCH\"] = branch\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ITERATION\"] = str(iteration)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\"] = str(feedback_path)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG\"] = json.dumps(adapter_config)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_STAGE\"] = \"build\"\n            env[\"ATTAVO_EVENTS\"] = str(events_path)\n            if checks_command:\n                env[\"ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND\"] = checks_command\n            env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n            env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n            env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n            env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n\n            run = subprocess.run([str(adapter_path)], cwd=str(root), env=env,\n                                 capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n            transcript, payload = split_adapter_stdout(run.stdout)\n            if run.returncode != 0:\n                # The guarantee behind issue #53's refusal: an adapter that\n                # exits non-zero always leaves a non-empty log, even one\n                # that printed nothing at all on stderr.\n                detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n                if run.stderr.strip():\n                    detail += \"\\n\" + run.stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n                transcript = (transcript + \"\\n\" if transcript else \"\") + detail\n            transcripts.append(transcript)\n\n            if run.returncode != 0 or payload is None or not payload.get(\"model\"):\n                status_out = \"failed\"\n                break\n\n            adapter_version = payload.get(\"adapter_version\")\n            model = payload.get(\"model\")\n            model_version = payload.get(\"model_version\")\n            tok = payload.get(\"tokens\") or {}\n            tokens[\"input\"] += tok.get(\"input\", 0) or 0\n            tokens[\"output\"] += tok.get(\"output\", 0) or 0\n            iter_cost = payload.get(\"cost_usd\")\n            if iter_cost is not None:\n                cost_usd = (cost_usd or 0) + iter_cost\n\n            if payload.get(\"status\") == \"question\":\n                status_out = \"halted\"\n                halted = {\"question\": payload.get(\"question\")}\n                break\n\n            foreign = next((c for c in commits_since(root, start_sha)\n                           if c[\"name\"] != identity[\"name\"] or c[\"email\"] != identity[\"email\"]),\n                          None)\n            if foreign:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = f\"commit {foreign['sha']} not authored by the executor\"\n                break\n\n            protected = protected_path_touched(root, start_sha, records_rel, specs_rel)\n            if protected:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = protected\n                refusal_provenance = \"executor\"\n                break\n\n            touched = sorted(changed_paths(root, start_sha, records_rel))\n            bad_path = next((p for p in touched if not matches_a_claim(p, claims)), None)\n            if bad_path:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = bad_path\n                break\n\n            criteria_results = [\n                {\"name\": name, \"exit\": run_criterion(spec_dir / \"criteria\" / name, root)}\n                for name in criteria_names]\n            for c in criteria_results:\n                append_event(events_path, \"gate\", f\"{c['name']}: exit {c['exit']}\")\n\n            select_in = \"\".join(p + \"\\n\" for p in touched)\n            select_run = subprocess.run(tests_cfg[\"select\"], shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                        input=select_in, capture_output=True,\n                                        text=True, check=False)\n            identifiers = [l for l in select_run.stdout.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n            run_in = \"\".join(i + \"\\n\" for i in identifiers)\n            test_run = subprocess.run(tests_cfg[\"run\"], shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                      input=run_in, capture_output=True,\n                                      text=True, check=False)\n            selected_tests = {\"select\": tests_cfg[\"select\"], \"run\": tests_cfg[\"run\"],\n                              \"count\": len(identifiers), \"exit\": test_run.returncode}\n\n            checks_run = None\n            if checks_command:\n                checks_run = subprocess.run(checks_command, shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                            capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n                checks_result = {\"command\": checks_command, \"exit\": checks_run.returncode}\n\n            # Issue #89, rejection test 1: the gate output that decides pass\n            # or fail is appended to the build log itself, under a heading\n            # per iteration, before this temporary directory goes away --\n            # tenant zero's #576 build-11 and #659 build-01 are a failed\n            # record with nothing beside it to say what was red, because\n            # this output previously lived only in feedback.txt, in a\n            # tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() cmd_build deletes on return.\n            gate_lines = [f\"criterion {c['name']}: exit {c['exit']}\" for c in criteria_results]\n            gate_lines.append(f\"selected tests ({selected_tests['count']}): exit \"\n                              f\"{selected_tests['exit']}\")\n            if test_run.stdout.strip():\n                gate_lines += [\"--- selected tests stdout ---\", test_run.stdout.rstrip(\"\\n\")]\n            if test_run.stderr.strip():\n                gate_lines += [\"--- selected tests stderr ---\", test_run.stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\")]\n            if checks_run is not None:\n                tail = (checks_run.stdout.splitlines() + checks_run.stderr.splitlines())\n                tail = tail[-CHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES:]\n                gate_lines.append(f\"tenant checks: exit {checks_run.returncode}\")\n                gate_lines += [\"--- checks output (tail) ---\", *tail]\n            transcripts[-1] += (f\"\\n--- attavo gates, iteration {iteration} ---\\n\"\n                               + \"\\n\".join(gate_lines))\n\n            failing = [c for c in criteria_results if c[\"exit\"] != 0]\n            checks_ok = checks_run is None or checks_run.returncode == 0\n            if not failing and test_run.returncode == 0 and checks_ok:\n                status_out = \"pass\"\n                break\n\n            if iteration == BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET:\n                status_out = \"failed\"\n                break\n\n            feedback_lines = []\n            if failing:\n                feedback_lines.append(\"criteria failing:\")\n                feedback_lines += [f\"- {c['name']}: exit {c['exit']}\" for c in failing]\n            if test_run.returncode != 0:\n                feedback_lines += [f\"test run exit {test_run.returncode}\",\n                                   \"--- stdout ---\", test_run.stdout,\n                                   \"--- stderr ---\", test_run.stderr]\n            if checks_run is not None and checks_run.returncode != 0:\n                tail = (checks_run.stdout.splitlines() + checks_run.stderr.splitlines())\n                tail = tail[-CHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES:]\n                feedback_lines += [f\"checks exit {checks_run.returncode}\",\n                                   \"--- checks output (tail) ---\", *tail]\n            feedback_path.write_text(\"\\n\".join(feedback_lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n    record = {\n        \"sha\": git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip(),\n        \"start_sha\": start_sha,\n        \"spec_sha\": spec_sha,\n        \"approval_sha\": latest_approval.get(\"sha\") if latest_approval else None,\n        \"at\": now_iso(),\n        \"adapter\": adapter_name,\n        \"adapter_config\": adapter_config,\n        \"executor_identity\": identity,\n        \"reports\": reports,\n        \"adapter_version\": adapter_version,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"model_version\": model_version,\n        \"iterations\": iterations_used,\n        \"criteria\": criteria_results,\n        \"selected_tests\": selected_tests,\n        \"checks\": checks_result,\n        \"tokens\": tokens,\n        \"cost_usd\": cost_usd,\n        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n        \"status\": status_out,\n        \"refusal\": refusal,\n        \"halted\": halted,\n        \"stop\": derive_stop(status_out, refusal=refusal, halted=halted,\n                            log=\"\\n\".join(transcripts),\n                            report_class=(payload or {}).get(\"class\"),\n                            refusal_provenance=refusal_provenance),\n    }\n    record_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"build\", record, m, item_id,\n                               log=\"\\n\".join(transcripts))\n\n    print(f\"attavo build: {status_out} ({record_path.name})\")\n    if status_out == \"halted\":\n        return BUILD_HALT_EXIT\n    return 0 if status_out == \"pass\" else 1\n\n\n# --- verify: the forge's own read first, a judge only once it is green ---\n\nFORGE_OK_CONCLUSIONS = {\"success\", \"neutral\", \"skipped\"}\n# issue #84: a concluded check's second token is a conclusion --\n# FORGE_OK_CONCLUSIONS, or another concluded one such as failure,\n# cancelled, or timed_out; an unconcluded check's is a status instead,\n# one of these. drive's own poll (poll_forge_checks) is the one reader\n# that needs to tell a still-running check apart from a concluded, not-ok\n# one -- read_forge_checks itself only ever needed \"green or not\".\nFORGE_UNCONCLUDED_STATUSES = {\"queued\", \"in_progress\", \"pending\", \"waiting\"}\n\n\ndef read_forge_checks(root: Path, checks_command: str, sha: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Runs the tenant's [forge].checks_command on sha; the product does\n    not know what forge that command reads. One line per check as\n    \"<name> <conclusion>\"; a command that fails to run, or any conclusion\n    other than success/neutral/skipped, is not green.\"\"\"\n    run = subprocess.run(f\"{checks_command} {shlex.quote(sha)}\", shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    conclusions = []\n    for line in run.stdout.splitlines():\n        line = line.strip()\n        if not line:\n            continue\n        parts = line.rsplit(\" \", 1)\n        if len(parts) == 2:\n            conclusions.append({\"name\": parts[0], \"conclusion\": parts[1]})\n    # A commit the forge has no record of is not green -- it is unread.\n    # The executor's own commit is exactly this: the forge attaches\n    # checks to a pull request's head, and that commit stops being the\n    # head the moment a record commit lands on top of it. all() over an\n    # empty list is True, which is why this is spelled out rather than\n    # implied by the loop above.\n    ok = run.returncode == 0 and bool(conclusions) and all(\n        c[\"conclusion\"] in FORGE_OK_CONCLUSIONS for c in conclusions)\n    return {\"command\": checks_command, \"sha\": sha, \"conclusions\": conclusions}, ok\n\n\ndef diff_since_approval(root: Path, approval_sha: str | None) -> tuple[str, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(diff_text, refusal): the item's own work since approval, not\n    everything merged onto the branch since then (issue #52) -- a\n    three-dot diff against approval_sha itself is not enough, since\n    approval_sha is already an ancestor of HEAD in the normal flow and\n    merge-base(approval_sha, HEAD) is just approval_sha again (verified\n    empirically, see issue #52). Diffing from the merge-base of HEAD and\n    the remote's default branch instead excludes content that arrived by\n    merging that branch in, because that content is already present on\n    both sides of the merge base. refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is what names\n    the default branch without hard-coding \"main\"; when it is not set,\n    there is nothing to diff against and this refuses rather than guess.\n    (\"\", None) when approval_sha is falsy -- nothing to diff from at all.\n    Shared by cmd_verify and cmd_counsel, which both hand an adapter this\n    same diff.\"\"\"\n    if not approval_sha:\n        return \"\", None\n    symref = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if symref.returncode != 0:\n        return \"\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; run `git remote set-head origin -a`\"\n    diff_base = git(root, \"merge-base\", symref.stdout.strip(), \"HEAD\").strip()\n    return git(root, \"diff\", diff_base, \"HEAD\"), None\n\n\ndef cmd_verify(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo verify: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    latest_build = latest_record(item_records_dir, \"build\")\n    if latest_build is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: no build record for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n    if latest_build.get(\"status\") != \"pass\":\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: latest build record is \"\n              f\"{latest_build.get('status')!r}, not pass\")\n        return 1\n\n    forge_cfg = m.get(\"forge\") or {}\n    checks_command = forge_cfg.get(\"checks_command\")\n    if not checks_command:\n        print(\"attavo verify: refused: no [forge].checks_command in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n\n    build_sha = latest_build[\"sha\"]\n    build_record_path = latest_attempt_path(item_records_dir, \"build\")\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    head_sha = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    # The forge attaches checks to a pull request's head, not to the\n    # executor's own commit -- that commit stops being the head the\n    # moment a record commit lands on top of it (issue #44). Reading the\n    # forge on head_sha is what the forge actually checked and what will\n    # be merged; build_sha and forge_checks[\"sha\"] can differ, and both\n    # are kept on the record rather than one sha serving two purposes.\n    forge_checks, forge_ok = read_forge_checks(root, checks_command, head_sha)\n\n    if not forge_ok:\n        record = {\n            \"sha\": head_sha,\n            \"build_sha\": build_sha,\n            \"build_record\": build_record_path.stem if build_record_path else None,\n            \"approval_sha\": latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\"),\n            \"at\": now_iso(),\n            \"adapter\": None, \"adapter_config\": {}, \"adapter_version\": None,\n            \"model\": None, \"model_version\": None,\n            \"reports\": [],\n            \"forge_checks\": forge_checks,\n            \"findings\": None,\n            \"tests_named\": [],\n            \"commits\": [],\n            \"mutation\": None, \"weak_stub\": False, \"stub_ratio\": None,\n            \"tokens\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0}, \"cost_usd\": None,\n            \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n            \"status\": \"returned\",\n            \"stop\": derive_stop(\"returned\"),\n        }\n        record_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"verify\", record, m, item_id)\n        print(f\"attavo verify: returned ({record_path.name}); the forge checks are not green\")\n        return 0\n\n    executor = m.get(\"executor\") or {}\n    adapter_name = executor.get(\"verify\") or executor.get(\"build\")\n    if not adapter_name:\n        print(\"attavo verify: refused: no [executor].verify or [executor].build in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n    adapter_path = resolve_adapter(root, adapter_name)\n    if adapter_path is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: no adapter named {adapter_name!r}\")\n        return 1\n\n    adapter_config = merge_adapter_config(m, adapter_name, \"verify\")\n    reports = adapter_reports(adapter_path)\n    approval_sha = latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\")\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    branch = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n\n    diff_text, diff_refusal = diff_since_approval(root, approval_sha)\n    if diff_refusal:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: {diff_refusal}\")\n        return 1\n\n    events_path = stage_events_dir(root) / f\"verify-{next_attempt_number(item_records_dir, 'verify'):02d}.events.jsonl\"\n\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        diff_path = Path(tmp) / \"diff.patch\"\n        diff_path.write_text(diff_text)\n\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"] = str(spec_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR\"] = str(item_records_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\"] = str(root / m[\"paths\"][\"rulings\"])\n        env[\"ATTAVO_BRANCH\"] = branch\n        env[\"ATTAVO_STAGE\"] = \"verify\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_DIFF\"] = str(diff_path)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_BUILD_RECORD\"] = str(build_record_path) if build_record_path else \"\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG\"] = json.dumps(adapter_config)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_EVENTS\"] = str(events_path)\n\n        run = subprocess.run([str(adapter_path)], cwd=str(root), env=env,\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n        transcript, payload = split_adapter_stdout(run.stdout)\n        if run.returncode != 0:\n            # Same guarantee as cmd_build's, issue #53: a non-zero adapter\n            # exit always leaves a non-empty log.\n            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n            if run.stderr.strip():\n                detail += \"\\n\" + run.stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n            transcript = (transcript + \"\\n\" if transcript else \"\") + detail\n\n    # Verify is a report, not a commit (issue #46): the adapter is invoked\n    # on the branch head it was handed, and must leave that head alone.\n    # Checked by comparing the head before the invocation (head_sha,\n    # already read above for the forge) against the head after it.\n    post_adapter_head = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    commits: list[str] = []\n    if post_adapter_head != head_sha:\n        commits = git(root, \"rev-list\", f\"{head_sha}..{post_adapter_head}\", \"--reverse\").split()\n\n    status_out = \"failed\"\n    findings = None\n    tests_named: list[str] = []\n    model = model_version = adapter_version_out = None\n    tokens = {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0}\n    cost_usd = None\n\n    if run.returncode == 0 and payload is not None and payload.get(\"model\"):\n        model = payload.get(\"model\")\n        model_version = payload.get(\"model_version\")\n        adapter_version_out = payload.get(\"adapter_version\")\n        tok = payload.get(\"tokens\") or {}\n        tokens = {\"input\": tok.get(\"input\", 0) or 0, \"output\": tok.get(\"output\", 0) or 0}\n        cost_usd = payload.get(\"cost_usd\")\n        # \"findings\" absent (or explicitly null) is not the same as an\n        # empty list: the adapter had no channel to report one at all,\n        # which is not a clean bill of health (issue #46). A commit\n        # during verify fails the attempt regardless of what it reported.\n        if not commits and \"findings\" in payload and payload[\"findings\"] is not None:\n            findings = payload[\"findings\"]\n            tests_named = payload.get(\"tests_named\") or []\n            status_out = \"pass\"\n\n    record = {\n        \"sha\": head_sha,\n        \"build_sha\": build_sha,\n        \"build_record\": build_record_path.stem if build_record_path else None,\n        \"approval_sha\": approval_sha,\n        \"at\": now_iso(),\n        \"adapter\": adapter_name,\n        \"adapter_config\": adapter_config,\n        \"adapter_version\": adapter_version_out,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"model_version\": model_version,\n        \"reports\": reports,\n        \"forge_checks\": forge_checks,\n        \"findings\": findings,\n        \"tests_named\": tests_named,\n        \"commits\": commits,\n        \"mutation\": None, \"weak_stub\": False, \"stub_ratio\": None,\n        \"tokens\": tokens,\n        \"cost_usd\": cost_usd,\n        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n        \"status\": status_out,\n        \"stop\": derive_stop(status_out, log=transcript,\n                            report_class=(payload or {}).get(\"class\")),\n    }\n    record_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"verify\", record, m, item_id, log=transcript)\n\n    print(f\"attavo verify: {status_out} ({record_path.name})\")\n    return 0 if status_out == \"pass\" else 1\n\n\n# --- counsel: a stop is read inside the product first, before a person\n# (issue #100). Read-only -- it commits nothing and writes nothing outside\n# paths.records/<N>/ -- and it never acts: it proposes a ruling, a patch,\n# or names the one-line question a person must answer. ---\n\nCOUNSEL_STAGES = (\"build\", \"verify\")\n\n\ndef latest_non_pass_stage_record(records_dir: Path) -> tuple[str | None, dict | None, Path | None]:\n    \"\"\"(stage, record, path) for the item's most recent non-pass build or\n    verify record, by its own \"at\" timestamp -- or, when neither stage\n    carries one, the item's latest refused spec-gate record (issue #133):\n    a refused gate is the same shape of stop, earlier, and it is read only\n    once a build or verify record exists to counsel first, since either\n    one already implies the gate that produced it passed. (None, None,\n    None) when none of the three exists. \"Most recent\" rather than\n    \"build, else verify\" so a stop on the stage that ran later (typically\n    verify, bound to a build that already passed) is the one counseled.\"\"\"\n    candidates: list[tuple[str, dict, Path]] = []\n    for stage in COUNSEL_STAGES:\n        path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, stage)\n        if path is None:\n            continue\n        rec = latest_record(records_dir, stage)\n        if rec.get(\"status\") == \"pass\":\n            continue\n        candidates.append((stage, rec, path))\n    if candidates:\n        candidates.sort(key=lambda c: c[1].get(\"at\") or \"\")\n        return candidates[-1]\n    spec_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"spec\")\n    if spec_path is not None:\n        spec_rec = latest_record(records_dir, \"spec\")\n        if spec_rec.get(\"status\") == \"refused\":\n            return \"spec\", spec_rec, spec_path\n    return None, None, None\n\n\ndef cmd_counsel(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo counsel: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    stage, stop_record, record_path = latest_non_pass_stage_record(item_records_dir)\n    if stop_record is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate record \"\n              f\"for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n\n    executor = m.get(\"executor\") or {}\n    adapter_name = executor.get(\"counsel\") or executor.get(\"verify\")\n    if not adapter_name:\n        print(\"attavo counsel: refused: no [executor].counsel or [executor].verify \"\n              \"in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n    adapter_path = resolve_adapter(root, adapter_name)\n    if adapter_path is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: no adapter named {adapter_name!r}\")\n        return 1\n\n    adapter_config = merge_adapter_config(m, adapter_name, \"counsel\")\n    reports = adapter_reports(adapter_path)\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    log_path = record_path.with_suffix(\".log\")\n\n    diff_text, diff_refusal = diff_since_approval(root, stop_record.get(\"approval_sha\"))\n    if diff_refusal:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: {diff_refusal}\")\n        return 1\n\n    started = time.monotonic()\n\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        diff_path = Path(tmp) / \"diff.patch\"\n        diff_path.write_text(diff_text)\n\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"] = str(spec_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR\"] = str(item_records_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\"] = str(root / m[\"paths\"][\"rulings\"])\n        env[\"ATTAVO_STAGE\"] = \"counsel\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_RECORD\"] = str(record_path)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_LOG\"] = str(log_path) if log_path.is_file() else \"\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_DIFF\"] = str(diff_path)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_MANIFEST\"] = str(root / MANIFEST)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_PRODUCT_ROOT\"] = str(PRODUCT_ROOT)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG\"] = json.dumps(adapter_config)\n\n        run = subprocess.run([str(adapter_path)], cwd=str(root), env=env,\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n        transcript, payload = split_adapter_stdout(run.stdout)\n        if run.returncode != 0:\n            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n            if run.stderr.strip():\n                detail += \"\\n\" + run.stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n            transcript = (transcript + \"\\n\" if transcript else \"\") + detail\n\n    status_out = \"failed\"\n    model = model_version = adapter_version_out = None\n    tokens = {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0}\n    cost_usd = None\n    cls = verdict = None\n    citations: list = []\n    proposal = {\"ruling_text\": None, \"patch\": None, \"question\": None}\n\n    if (run.returncode == 0 and payload is not None\n            and payload.get(\"verdict\") in (\"answer\", \"patch\", \"person\")):\n        status_out = \"done\"\n        model = payload.get(\"model\")\n        model_version = payload.get(\"model_version\")\n        adapter_version_out = payload.get(\"adapter_version\")\n        tok = payload.get(\"tokens\") or {}\n        tokens = {\"input\": tok.get(\"input\", 0) or 0, \"output\": tok.get(\"output\", 0) or 0}\n        cost_usd = payload.get(\"cost_usd\")\n        cls = payload.get(\"class\")\n        verdict = payload.get(\"verdict\")\n        citations = payload.get(\"citations\") or []\n        proposal = payload.get(\"proposal\") or proposal\n\n    record = {\n        \"sha\": git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip(),\n        \"record_stage\": stage,\n        \"record\": record_path.stem,\n        \"at\": now_iso(),\n        \"adapter\": adapter_name,\n        \"adapter_config\": adapter_config,\n        \"adapter_version\": adapter_version_out,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"model_version\": model_version,\n        \"reports\": reports,\n        \"tokens\": tokens,\n        \"cost_usd\": cost_usd,\n        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n        \"status\": status_out,\n        \"class\": cls,\n        \"verdict\": verdict,\n        \"citations\": citations,\n        \"proposal\": proposal,\n    }\n    record_out_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"counsel\", record, m, item_id, log=transcript)\n\n    print(f\"attavo counsel: {status_out} ({record_out_path.name})\")\n    return 0 if status_out == \"done\" else 1\n\n\n# --- drive: the mechanical transitions between approval and ready-to-merge\n# (issue #84) -- one step per invocation, and only that step, until a\n# state that belongs to a person. Writes no record of its own; the stage\n# records already on disk are the only state it reads. ---\n\ndef forge_checks_unconcluded(forge_checks: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether poll_forge_checks should keep waiting rather than stop at\n    once: an empty read (the forge has not attached any check to this sha\n    yet) or any one check still carrying a status (queued, in_progress,\n    pending, waiting) rather than a concluded conclusion. A concluded\n    conclusion that is not green (failure, cancelled, timed_out, and\n    anything else read_forge_checks did not recognize as ok) is not this\n    -- that check is done, whether or not it passed.\"\"\"\n    conclusions = forge_checks[\"conclusions\"]\n    if not conclusions:\n        return True\n    return any(c[\"conclusion\"] in FORGE_UNCONCLUDED_STATUSES for c in conclusions)\n\n\ndef poll_forge_checks(root: Path, checks_command: str, sha: str) -> tuple[dict, bool]:\n    \"\"\"read_forge_checks, retried within drive_forge_poll_bound_s() while\n    some check is still unconcluded (forge_checks_unconcluded) -- a check\n    still running is not yet red, and drive gives it a little room to\n    conclude before it gives up. A read where every check has already\n    concluded, green or not, stops here at once: there is nothing left to\n    wait on. The bound and interval are constants this lane names, not a\n    manifest key, re-read at call time so a test's own clock\n    (ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S, ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S) never has to\n    survive past when it was set.\"\"\"\n    bound = drive_forge_poll_bound_s()\n    interval = drive_forge_poll_interval_s()\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + bound\n    forge_checks, ok = read_forge_checks(root, checks_command, sha)\n    while not ok and forge_checks_unconcluded(forge_checks) and time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        time.sleep(interval)\n        forge_checks, ok = read_forge_checks(root, checks_command, sha)\n    return forge_checks, ok\n\n\ndef commit_record(root: Path, record_paths: Path | list[Path], message: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"`git commit --only` on every record path given, and each one's .log\n    and .filed, each if one exists -- never the whole index. A transport\n    commit that sweeps the index is exactly the regression issue #46\n    already guards build and verify against on the adapter side; drive\n    must not reintroduce it on the transport side. The .filed marker\n    (issue #89) is committed alongside the record it names, in the same\n    commit and the same push, so a second worktree or a fresh clone reads\n    the same filed fact rather than refiling every stop it finds with no\n    marker of its own. A single Path is accepted for the common one-record\n    case; issue #100 passes a list so the counsel record lands in the same\n    commit as the stage record it counsels. Authored and committed as\n    driver_identity(), set by the product and never the tenant's git\n    config, so a driven item's record commits are never indistinguishable\n    from an operator's own.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(record_paths, Path):\n        record_paths = [record_paths]\n    paths: list[str] = []\n    for record_path in record_paths:\n        paths.append(str(record_path.relative_to(root)))\n        log_path = record_path.with_suffix(\".log\")\n        if log_path.is_file():\n            paths.append(str(log_path.relative_to(root)))\n        marker_path = record_path.with_suffix(\".filed\")\n        if marker_path.is_file():\n            paths.append(str(marker_path.relative_to(root)))\n    identity = driver_identity()\n    env = dict(os.environ)\n    env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n    env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n    env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n    env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n    git(root, \"add\", *paths)\n    git(root, \"commit\", \"--only\", \"-m\", message, *paths, env=env)\n\n\ndef push_record_commit(root: Path, branch: str) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"Push HEAD to branch on origin. A push a divergent remote rejects is\n    retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit origin branch` -- a\n    merge, never a rebase, because a rebase would change the sha the record\n    commit just wrote already names.\"\"\"\n    def attempt() -> tuple[bool, str]:\n        run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"push\", \"origin\", f\"HEAD:{branch}\"],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n        return run.returncode == 0, run.stderr.strip()\n\n    ok, err = attempt()\n    if ok:\n        return True, None\n    pull = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"pull\", \"--no-rebase\", \"--no-edit\",\n                           \"origin\", branch], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if pull.returncode != 0:\n        return False, f\"push rejected and the retry merge failed: {pull.stderr.strip() or err}\"\n    ok, err = attempt()\n    if not ok:\n        return False, f\"push rejected again after merging {branch}: {err}\"\n    return True, None\n\n\ndef drive_state(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> tuple[str, str | None, Path]:\n    \"\"\"(\"no-approval\" | \"build\" | \"verify\" | \"ready\", detail, records_dir):\n    the next mechanical step for item_id, read from its latest records\n    alone. A build only counts as current when it is a pass bound to the\n    valid approval's own sha; a verify only counts as current when it is a\n    pass bound to that build's own sha -- the same staleness a re-approval\n    or a re-build must force, attest's own chain check already enforces\n    (check_attest_chain), read here rather than re-typed.\"\"\"\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    status = approval_status(root, m, item_id)\n    if status != \"valid\":\n        return \"no-approval\", status, records_dir\n\n    latest_approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\")\n    latest_build = latest_record(records_dir, \"build\")\n    build_current = (latest_build is not None and latest_build.get(\"status\") == \"pass\"\n                     and latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\") == (latest_approval or {}).get(\"sha\"))\n    if not build_current:\n        return \"build\", None, records_dir\n\n    latest_verify = latest_record(records_dir, \"verify\")\n    verify_current = (latest_verify is not None and latest_verify.get(\"status\") == \"pass\"\n                      and latest_verify.get(\"build_sha\") == latest_build.get(\"sha\"))\n    if not verify_current:\n        return \"verify\", None, records_dir\n\n    return \"ready\", None, records_dir\n\n\ndef _drive_run_stage(root: Path, records_dir: Path, branch: str, stage: str, item_id: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Runs build or verify in-process -- the same command `attavo build`\n    or `attavo verify` would run, printing the same reason on a refusal,\n    failure, or halt. A non-pass record is counseled (cmd_counsel, issue\n    #100) and filed (cmd_file_stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\n    so a stop's own counsel record and .filed marker -- the filing\n    command's stdout, the issue file-stops just opened -- exist on disk\n    in time to be committed and pushed in the very same commit as the\n    stage record and its log; a marker written only after the push would\n    never reach the ledger at all, and a second worktree or a fresh clone\n    would refile every stop it finds with no marker beside it. The stage\n    record and the counsel record (when one was written) are then\n    transported together: committed with commit_record and pushed with\n    push_record_commit, whatever the stage record's status -- the record\n    pushes stay the same pushes, made by drive in the run that produced\n    the record (issue #84's rule 42 row).\"\"\"\n    before = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, stage)\n    # The invocation's marker, committed and pushed before the stage runs:\n    # one commit per attempt, so that an invocation which dies or hangs\n    # is a fact on the branch (proof five) and not a silence.\n    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\n    marker = write_invocation_marker(root, records_dir, stage, nn)\n    try:\n        commit_record(root, [marker], f\"attavo: {stage} invocation {nn:02d} started for item {item_id}\")\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {stage} invocation marker: {exc}\")\n        return 1\n    ok, err = push_record_commit(root, branch)\n    if not ok:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not push the {stage} invocation marker: {err}\")\n        return 1\n    rc = cmd_build([item_id]) if stage == \"build\" else cmd_verify([item_id])\n    after = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, stage)\n\n    if after is None or after == before:\n        # Refused before writing anything at all (e.g. no adapter\n        # configured) -- the stage command already printed why.\n        return rc if rc != 0 else 1\n\n    record = latest_record(records_dir, stage)\n    status_out = record.get(\"status\")\n    to_commit = [after]\n    if status_out != \"pass\":\n        counsel_before = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"counsel\")\n        cmd_counsel([item_id])\n        counsel_after = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"counsel\")\n        if counsel_after is not None and counsel_after != counsel_before:\n            to_commit.append(counsel_after)\n        # file-stops is its own idempotent read of the item's records, so\n        # calling it here on every run that wrote a non-pass record is\n        # safe to call again on a later run: an already-filed stop's own\n        # marker is what stops it from being filed twice.\n        cmd_file_stops([item_id])\n\n    message = f\"attavo: {stage} record for item {item_id} ({after.stem})\"\n    try:\n        commit_record(root, to_commit, message)\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {stage} record: {exc}\")\n        return 1\n\n    ok, err = push_record_commit(root, branch)\n    if not ok:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not push the {stage} record: {err}\")\n        return 1\n\n    if status_out == \"halted\":\n        question = (record.get(\"halted\") or {}).get(\"question\")\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {stage} halted: {question} ({after.name}); \"\n              f\"pushed to {branch}\")\n    elif status_out != \"pass\":\n        reason = record.get(\"refusal\") or status_out\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {stage} {status_out}: {reason} ({after.name}); \"\n              f\"pushed to {branch}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: pushed {after.name} to {branch}\")\n    return rc\n\n\ndef _drive_step(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> tuple[int, bool]:\n    \"\"\"One mechanical step, exactly as a single `attavo drive` call always\n    has -- and whether repetition under --until-ready should stop here:\n    True for every refusal or stop (no valid approval, no\n    [forge].checks_command, the forge not green, or a stage that wrote a\n    non-pass record) and for the ready-to-merge terminal state; False\n    only when a stage just passed, so drive_state may have a further\n    stage to pursue on the next call.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        stage, extra, records_dir = drive_state(root, m, item_id)\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2, True\n\n    if stage == \"no-approval\":\n        print(f\"attavo drive: refused: approval is {extra}\")\n        return 1, True\n\n    branch = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n\n    if stage == \"build\":\n        rc = _drive_run_stage(root, records_dir, branch, \"build\", item_id)\n        return rc, rc != 0\n\n    checks_command = (m.get(\"forge\") or {}).get(\"checks_command\")\n    if not checks_command:\n        print(\"attavo drive: refused: no [forge].checks_command in the manifest\")\n        return 1, True\n    head_sha = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n    forge_checks, ok = poll_forge_checks(root, checks_command, head_sha)\n    if not ok:\n        conclusions = (\", \".join(f\"{c['name']} {c['conclusion']}\"\n                                 for c in forge_checks[\"conclusions\"])\n                      or \"no checks reported\")\n        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: forge checks not green on {head_sha[:12]}: {conclusions}\")\n        return 1, True\n\n    if stage == \"verify\":\n        rc = _drive_run_stage(root, records_dir, branch, \"verify\", item_id)\n        return rc, rc != 0\n\n    print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id} is ready to merge\")\n    return 0, True\n\n\ndef cmd_drive(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    until_ready = \"--until-ready\" in argv\n    recover = \"--recover\" in argv\n    positional = [a for a in argv if a not in (\"--until-ready\", \"--recover\")]\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = positional[0] if positional else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo drive: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo drive: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    if recover:\n        return _drive_recover(root, m, item_id)\n\n    # Without --until-ready this is exactly one call to _drive_step,\n    # letter for letter what cmd_drive always did: `not until_ready`\n    # returns on the very first iteration regardless of `done`. With it,\n    # a step that just passed (done False) repeats -- step, wait (the\n    # forge poll already inside _drive_step), step, wait -- until the\n    # item is ready to merge or a step stops on its own account.\n    while True:\n        rc, done = _drive_step(root, m, item_id)\n        if done or not until_ready:\n            return rc\n\n\n# --- file-findings: one tenant issue per finding, nothing filed silently ---\n\ndef cmd_file_findings(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo file-findings: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo file-findings: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    forge_cfg = m.get(\"forge\") or {}\n    file_issue_command = forge_cfg.get(\"file_issue_command\")\n    if not file_issue_command:\n        print(\"attavo file-findings: refused: no [forge].file_issue_command in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n\n    latest_verify = latest_record(item_records_dir, \"verify\")\n    if latest_verify is None:\n        print(f\"attavo file-findings: refused: no verify record for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n\n    findings = latest_verify.get(\"findings\") or []\n    if not findings:\n        print(\"attavo file-findings: no findings to file\")\n        return 0\n\n    for finding in findings:\n        if not finding.get(\"retires\"):\n            title = finding.get(\"title\", \"<untitled>\")\n            print(f\"attavo file-findings: refused: finding {title!r} carries no retires; \"\n                  f\"nothing filed\")\n            return 1\n\n    for finding in findings:\n        run = subprocess.run(file_issue_command, shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                             input=json.dumps(finding) + \"\\n\", capture_output=True,\n                             text=True, check=False)\n        if run.returncode != 0:\n            title = finding.get(\"title\", \"<untitled>\")\n            print(f\"attavo file-findings: refused: filing {title!r} exited {run.returncode}: \"\n                  f\"{run.stderr.strip()}\")\n            return 1\n\n    print(f\"attavo file-findings: filed {len(findings)} issue(s)\")\n    return 0\n\n\n# --- file-stops: one tenant issue per stop record, nothing filed silently,\n# nothing filed twice (issue #89) ---\n\nSTOP_STAGES = (\"build\", \"verify\")\nFILE_STOPS_LOG_TAIL_LINES = 20\n\n\ndef compose_stop_title(item_id: str, stage: str, n: int, stop: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"`stop <class>/<provenance> on item <N>: <stage>-<NN>` -- the title\n    the tenant's file-issue script would otherwise fall back to\n    <untitled> for. An empty class or provenance is a record defect, not\n    a filing: this returns \"\" rather than a title with a blank half, so\n    the caller can refuse on it.\"\"\"\n    cls = stop.get(\"class\")\n    provenance = stop.get(\"provenance\")\n    if not cls or not provenance:\n        return \"\"\n    return f\"stop {cls}/{provenance} on item {item_id}: {stage}-{n:02d}\"\n\n\ndef counsel_record_for(item_records_dir: Path, stage: str, n: int) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The latest counsel-NN.json (issue #100) whose own \"record\" field\n    names f\"{stage}-{n:02d}\" -- the counsel invocation, if any, that read\n    this exact stage record -- or None when counsel never ran against it\n    (e.g. file-stops run standalone, outside drive).\"\"\"\n    target = f\"{stage}-{n:02d}\"\n    attempts = parse_attempts(item_records_dir, \"counsel\")\n    matches = [rec for _, rec in sorted(attempts.items()) if rec.get(\"record\") == target]\n    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n\n\ndef cmd_file_stops(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo file-stops: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo file-stops: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    forge_cfg = m.get(\"forge\") or {}\n    file_issue_command = forge_cfg.get(\"file_issue_command\")\n    if not file_issue_command:\n        print(\"attavo file-stops: refused: no [forge].file_issue_command in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n\n    # A stop record's own .filed marker beside it -- the same convention as\n    # its .log sidecar -- is what makes a second run file nothing: no new\n    # artifact beside the records (the gate output already lives in the\n    # log), just a fact about this one record, in the one place a reader\n    # already looks. It carries the filing command's own stdout (the\n    # issue it opened), so that fact is kept, not just the fact of\n    # filing. This command never commits it -- the same as build and\n    # verify, which write their own records uncommitted -- a caller that\n    # wants it on the ledger commits it itself; drive does, in the same\n    # commit as the record and its log (issue #89).\n    pending: list[tuple[str, int, dict, Path]] = []\n    for stage in STOP_STAGES:\n        attempts = parse_attempts(item_records_dir, stage)\n        for n in sorted(attempts):\n            stop = attempts[n].get(\"stop\")\n            if not stop:\n                continue\n            marker = item_records_dir / f\"{stage}-{n:02d}.filed\"\n            if marker.exists():\n                continue\n            pending.append((stage, n, stop, marker))\n\n    # A refused spec-gate record is the same shape of stop, earlier (issue\n    # #133); its own class is \"gate\" (issue #137), never persisted -- it\n    # never carries a stop field of its own (cmd_spec_gate is untouched\n    # by this lane), so it is synthesized here from its refusal.\n    for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_records_dir, \"spec\").items()):\n        if rec.get(\"status\") != \"refused\":\n            continue\n        marker = item_records_dir / f\"spec-{n:02d}.filed\"\n        if marker.exists():\n            continue\n        pending.append((\"spec\", n, gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\")), marker))\n\n    if not pending:\n        print(\"attavo file-stops: no stops to file\")\n        return 0\n\n    for stage, n, stop, _marker in pending:\n        if stop[\"class\"] == \"unclassed\" and not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: {stage}-{n:02d} is unclassed with no detail; \"\n                  f\"nothing filed\")\n            return 1\n\n    for stage, n, stop, _marker in pending:\n        if not compose_stop_title(item_id, stage, n, stop):\n            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: {stage}-{n:02d} composes an empty title; \"\n                  f\"nothing filed\")\n            return 1\n\n    for stage, n, stop, marker in pending:\n        record_path = item_records_dir / f\"{stage}-{n:02d}.json\"\n        log_path = record_path.with_suffix(\".log\")\n        log_tail = (\"\\n\".join(log_path.read_text().splitlines()[-FILE_STOPS_LOG_TAIL_LINES:])\n                   if log_path.is_file() else \"\")\n        counsel = counsel_record_for(item_records_dir, stage, n)\n        body = {\n            \"title\": compose_stop_title(item_id, stage, n, stop),\n            \"class\": stop[\"class\"],\n            \"provenance\": stop[\"provenance\"],\n            \"record\": str(record_path.relative_to(root)),\n            \"log_tail\": log_tail,\n            \"counsel_verdict\": counsel.get(\"verdict\") if counsel else None,\n            \"counsel_citations\": counsel.get(\"citations\") if counsel else [],\n            \"counsel_proposal\": counsel.get(\"proposal\") if counsel else None,\n        }\n        run = subprocess.run(file_issue_command, shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                             input=json.dumps(body) + \"\\n\", capture_output=True,\n                             text=True, check=False)\n        if run.returncode != 0:\n            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: filing {stage}-{n:02d} exited {run.returncode}: \"\n                  f\"{run.stderr.strip()}\")\n            return 1\n        marker.write_text(run.stdout)\n\n    print(f\"attavo file-stops: filed {len(pending)} issue(s)\")\n    return 0\n\n\n# --- record-only: whether HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\n# paths.records. Core logic about a git checkout, not a forge's shell\n# (issue #19); a workflow template's push-and-retrigger guard is one line\n# calling this instead of carrying its own copy. ---\n\ndef cmd_record_only(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo record-only: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    try:\n        changed = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD^1\", \"HEAD\").splitlines()\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        print(f\"attavo record-only: refused: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    prefix = records_rel.rstrip(\"/\") + \"/\"\n    only_records = all(p == records_rel or p.startswith(prefix) for p in changed if p)\n    print(\"attavo record-only: yes\" if only_records else \"attavo record-only: no\")\n    return 0 if only_records else 1\n\n\n# --- attest: the signed envelope over one item's whole traversal ---\n\ndef derive_attest_items(root: Path, records_rel: str) -> tuple[set[str], str | None]:\n    \"\"\"The item ids from the merge commit's own first-parent diff -- record\n    paths under records_rel/<N>/, not a branch name, which a squash merge\n    discards and which names a forge's convention the product does not\n    know. Returns (items, None), else (empty set, reason) only when the\n    diff itself could not be read -- zero items found is not an error\n    here (issue #58): not every merge is an item merge, and the caller\n    decides what zero, one, or more than one means.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        changed = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD^1\", \"HEAD\").splitlines()\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        return set(), f\"git: {exc}\"\n    prefix = records_rel.rstrip(\"/\") + \"/\"\n    items: set[str] = set()\n    for p in changed:\n        if p.startswith(prefix):\n            rest = p[len(prefix):]\n            item = rest.split(\"/\", 1)[0]\n            if item:\n                items.add(item)\n    return items, None\n\n\nNOT_YET = object()\n\n\ndef check_attest_chain(records_dir: Path, item_id: str, partial: bool = False):\n    \"\"\"The two assertions attavo attest refuses on: the latest spec,\n    approval, build, and verify records for item_id all exist, and\n    build's approval_sha names the latest approval -- a re-approval after\n    a build must force a re-run of what changed. Returns (None, message)\n    on either of them, the message being the same text attest prints, not\n    a copy of it a caller re-types (issue #74: proof two reuses it);\n    returns ((spec, approval, build, verify), None) when the chain holds.\n\n    A verify record can only name a build that existed when it was\n    written (issue #109), so a latest verify whose build_sha is not the\n    latest build's sha is never a corrupt chain -- it is a verify\n    superseded by a later build, and is treated as absent: the next\n    stage is verify, not a refusal, exactly as if no verify record\n    existed yet.\n\n    partial (issue #67) is for a pull request, where a later stage's\n    record cannot exist yet because the stage that would produce it is\n    itself waiting on this check. Under partial, a missing (or\n    superseded) record is not a refusal -- the chain assertion still\n    runs over whatever records exist, and (NOT_YET, message) is\n    returned, the message naming the item and the stages present and\n    absent -- or, for a superseded verify, the superseded record and the\n    build it named -- when a stage is still missing once that assertion\n    holds.\"\"\"\n    latest_spec = latest_record(records_dir, \"spec\")\n    latest_approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\")\n    latest_build = latest_record(records_dir, \"build\")\n    latest_verify = latest_record(records_dir, \"verify\")\n\n    # A verify naming a sha other than the latest build's is superseded:\n    # treated as absent for the chain, never as a mismatch.\n    superseded = None\n    if latest_build is not None and latest_verify is not None:\n        named_sha = latest_verify.get(\"build_sha\")\n        if named_sha != latest_build.get(\"sha\"):\n            verify_n = max(parse_attempts(records_dir, \"verify\"))\n            build_attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, \"build\")\n            named_build_n = next((n for n, rec in build_attempts.items()\n                                  if rec.get(\"sha\") == named_sha), None)\n            named_build = f\"build-{named_build_n:02d}\" if named_build_n is not None else named_sha\n            superseded = (verify_n, named_sha, named_build, max(build_attempts))\n            latest_verify = None\n\n    stages = ((\"spec\", latest_spec), (\"approval\", latest_approval),\n              (\"build\", latest_build), (\"verify\", latest_verify))\n\n    if not partial:\n        for stage, rec in stages:\n            if rec is None:\n                if stage == \"verify\" and superseded is not None:\n                    verify_n, named_sha, _, _ = superseded\n                    return None, (f\"no verify names the latest build \"\n                                 f\"(verify-{verify_n:02d} names {named_sha})\")\n                return None, f\"no {stage} record for item {item_id}\"\n\n    if latest_approval is not None and latest_build is not None:\n        if latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\") != latest_approval.get(\"sha\"):\n            return None, (\"build's approval_sha does not name the latest approval; a \"\n                          \"re-approval after the build must force a re-run\")\n\n    missing = [stage for stage, rec in stages if rec is None]\n    if partial and missing:\n        present = [stage for stage, rec in stages if rec is not None]\n        if missing == [\"verify\"] and superseded is not None:\n            verify_n, _, named_build, latest_build_n = superseded\n            return NOT_YET, (f\"item {item_id} not yet (present: {', '.join(present) or 'none'}; \"\n                             f\"verify-{verify_n:02d} names {named_build}, \"\n                             f\"superseded by build-{latest_build_n:02d})\")\n        return NOT_YET, (f\"item {item_id} not yet (present: {', '.join(present) or 'none'}; \"\n                         f\"absent: {', '.join(missing)})\")\n\n    return (latest_spec, latest_approval, latest_build, latest_verify), None\n\n\ndef cmd_attest(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    partial = \"--partial\" in argv\n    positional = [a for a in argv if not a.startswith(\"--\")]\n    unknown = [a for a in argv if a.startswith(\"--\") and a != \"--partial\"]\n    if unknown:\n        print(f\"attavo attest: unknown argument {unknown[0]!r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo attest: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_id = positional[0] if positional else None\n    if item_id is None:\n        items, err = derive_attest_items(root, records_rel)\n        if err:\n            print(f\"attavo attest: refused: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        # Not every merge is an item merge -- a merge that carries no item\n        # at all is an ordinary fact, not a defect (issue #58); the\n        # attest template runs this on every push and has nothing to\n        # sign or commit when nothing was attested, and its existing\n        # `if:` guards already read this step's own exit code.\n        if not items:\n            print(\"attavo attest: no item derived from the merge commit's record paths; \"\n                  \"nothing to attest\")\n            return 0\n        if len(items) > 1:\n            print(f\"attavo attest: refused: {len(items)} items derived from the merge \"\n                  f\"commit's record paths: {', '.join(sorted(items))}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        item_id = next(iter(items))\n\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    chain, message = check_attest_chain(records_dir, item_id, partial=partial)\n    if chain is None:\n        print(f\"attavo attest: refused: {message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    if chain is NOT_YET:\n        print(f\"attavo attest --partial: {message}\")\n        return 0\n    latest_spec, latest_approval, latest_build, latest_verify = chain\n\n    spec_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"spec\")\n    approval_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"approval\")\n    build_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"build\")\n    verify_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"verify\")\n\n    # sha and merge_sha are the same commit here -- the one this statement\n    # was computed at. On the merge group that commit is the one main will\n    # hold; kept as two fields because a forge-specific template signs\n    # this statement against \"the commit that lands\", naming it merge_sha\n    # is what makes that unambiguous to a reader who has never seen attest\n    # run anywhere but the merge group.\n    head_sha = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").strip()\n\n    statement = {\n        \"sha\": head_sha,\n        \"merge_sha\": head_sha,\n        \"item\": item_id,\n        \"spec\": spec_path.stem if spec_path else None,\n        \"spec_sha\": latest_spec.get(\"sha\"),\n        \"approval\": approval_path.stem if approval_path else None,\n        \"approval_sha\": latest_approval.get(\"sha\"),\n        \"build\": build_path.stem if build_path else None,\n        \"build_sha\": latest_build.get(\"sha\"),\n        \"verify\": verify_path.stem if verify_path else None,\n        \"verify_sha\": latest_verify.get(\"sha\"),\n        \"at\": now_iso(),\n        # Neither is populated by anything today -- no ruling or amendment\n        # log exists yet for either to read from. Carried as empty rather\n        # than omitted, since the schema names them.\n        \"interventions\": [],\n        \"acts\": [],\n        \"tokens_by_stage\": {\"build\": latest_build.get(\"tokens\"), \"verify\": latest_verify.get(\"tokens\")},\n        # Never summed across stages -- the 2026-09-09 ruling on reporting\n        # across vendors: a stage's executor may report no cost at all.\n        \"cost_by_stage_usd\": {\"build\": latest_build.get(\"cost_usd\"), \"verify\": latest_verify.get(\"cost_usd\")},\n        \"wall_clock_by_stage_s\": {\"build\": latest_build.get(\"wall_clock_s\"),\n                                  \"verify\": latest_verify.get(\"wall_clock_s\")},\n        \"product_version\": product_version(),\n        \"product_pin\": (m.get(\"attavo\") or {}).get(\"version\"),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(statement, indent=2))\n    return 0\n\n\n# --- ledger: every act on an item by identity and class (issue #128) ---\n\n# operator acts (a person's own decisions and transport) vs. product acts\n# (the driver's or the records app's own automated commits) vs. the\n# executor's own code changes -- the three totals the plan's status table\n# and every reviewing session used to count by hand. record-or-launch\n# (below) contributes to neither: an honest count never guesses which\n# side of that line a pre-v0.18.0 commit falls on.\nLEDGER_OPERATOR_CLASSES = (\"approve\", \"amend\", \"launch\", \"transport\", \"merge\")\nLEDGER_V018_CUTOFF = (0, 18, 0)\n\n\ndef _semver_tuple(version: str | None) -> tuple[int, int, int] | None:\n    m = re.match(r\"^v(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\", version or \"\")\n    return (int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2)), int(m.group(3))) if m else None\n\n\ndef _is_records_app(name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"The forge's own app-bot login -- exactly the identity the\n    attavo-spec-gate and attavo-approve templates commit spec-gate and\n    approval records as (an app-token step mints it at run time from the\n    tenant's own app credentials): \"<app-slug>[bot]\". Never a name this\n    product can name in advance, so the one fact it can check is the\n    shape the forge itself gives every app identity, not a specific one.\"\"\"\n    return name.endswith(\"[bot]\")\n\n\ndef first_commit_touching(root: Path, relpath: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The earliest commit touching relpath -- the mirror of\n    last_commit_touching, which answers the latest. Ledger's own walk\n    starts here: the item's first spec commit.\"\"\"\n    out = git(root, \"log\", \"--reverse\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", relpath)\n    lines = out.split()\n    return lines[0] if lines else None\n\n\ndef _commit_touches(root: Path, sha: str) -> list[str]:\n    return git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", f\"{sha}^1\", sha).splitlines()\n\n\ndef _record_at(root: Path, sha: str, relpath: str, item_id: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"A record's own dict at a past commit, not the working tree --\n    ledger's only need for one (issue #128). Read through _load_record\n    (issue #60, acceptance 6: the one place a record's bytes become a\n    dict) by spilling the blob to a throwaway file, rather than a second\n    json.loads of its own: `git show` has no path on disk to hand\n    _load_record directly.\"\"\"\n    out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"show\", f\"{sha}:{relpath}\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if out.returncode != 0:\n        return {}\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(\"w\", suffix=\".json\", delete=False) as fh:\n        fh.write(out.stdout)\n        blob_path = Path(fh.name)\n    try:\n        return _load_record(blob_path, item_id)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return {}\n    finally:\n        blob_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\n\ndef item_ledger(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"{\"item\", \"rows\", \"summary\"}: one row per act between item_id's first\n    spec commit and its merge (merge_introducing_records, the same\n    derivation doctor's proof two and attest both already read) or HEAD\n    when the item has not merged yet.\n\n    Each commit gets exactly one class, in this order: the merge commit\n    itself is \"merge\"; a commit authored by the executor identity\n    (executor_identity) is \"change\"; a commit introducing an approval\n    record is \"approve\", whoever committed it -- an operator's decision,\n    however it reached git; a commit introducing a spec-gate, build, or\n    verify record, authored by the driver identity (driver_identity) or\n    the records app, is \"record\"; the same, authored by a person, is\n    \"launch\" for build or verify (spec-gate records the app always\n    commits, in every template this product ships) -- unless that\n    record's own product_version predates v0.18.0, when driver_identity\n    did not yet exist to tell the two apart, and the row is\n    \"record-or-launch\" with a note, counted in neither summary total\n    rather than guessed; a person's commit touching the spec is \"spec\"\n    before the first approval record and \"amend\" after; anything else by\n    a person is \"transport\" (a merge of main among them).\"\"\"\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    specs_prefix = f\"{specs_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n    records_prefix = f\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n    empty_summary = {\"operator_acts\": 0, \"product_acts\": 0, \"executor_commits\": 0,\n                     \"stops\": 0, \"since\": None}\n\n    first_spec_sha = first_commit_touching(root, str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id))\n    if first_spec_sha is None:\n        return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": [], \"summary\": empty_summary}\n\n    merge_sha = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item_id, STAGES)\n    if merge_sha is not None:\n        branch_tip = git(root, \"rev-parse\", f\"{merge_sha}^2\").strip()\n        commits = commits_since(root, f\"{first_spec_sha}^\", end=branch_tip)\n        commits += commits_since(root, f\"{merge_sha}^1\", end=merge_sha)\n    else:\n        commits = commits_since(root, f\"{first_spec_sha}^\", end=\"HEAD\")\n\n    driver = driver_identity()\n    rows: list[dict] = []\n    operator_acts = product_acts = executor_commits = 0\n    since = None\n    approval_seen = False\n\n    for c in commits:\n        sha, name, email = c[\"sha\"], c[\"name\"], c[\"email\"]\n\n        if merge_sha is not None and sha == merge_sha:\n            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"merge\"})\n            operator_acts += 1\n            continue\n\n        if email.startswith(\"executor+\") and email.endswith(\"@attavo.invalid\"):\n            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"change\"})\n            executor_commits += 1\n            continue\n\n        touched = _commit_touches(root, sha)\n        record_touch = None\n        for p in touched:\n            if not p.startswith(records_prefix):\n                continue\n            rm = RECORD_RE.match(Path(p).name)\n            if rm and rm.group(1) in STAGES:\n                record_touch = (rm.group(1), p)\n                break\n\n        if record_touch is not None:\n            stage, relpath = record_touch\n            content = _record_at(root, sha, relpath, item_id)\n            if since is None:\n                since = content.get(\"product_version\")\n\n            if stage == \"approval\":\n                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"approve\"})\n                operator_acts += 1\n                approval_seen = True\n                continue\n\n            is_driver = name == driver[\"name\"] and email == driver[\"email\"]\n            is_records_app = _is_records_app(name)\n            if stage == \"spec\" or is_driver or is_records_app:\n                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"record\"})\n                product_acts += 1\n                continue\n\n            version = _semver_tuple(content.get(\"product_version\"))\n            if version is not None and version < LEDGER_V018_CUTOFF:\n                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"record-or-launch\",\n                            \"note\": \"not distinguishable before v0.18.0\"})\n                continue\n\n            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"launch\"})\n            operator_acts += 1\n            continue\n\n        # An invocation marker's own commit (proof five): the product's\n        # act, never the operator's.\n        if any(p.startswith(records_prefix) and p.endswith(INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX)\n               for p in touched):\n            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"record\"})\n            product_acts += 1\n            continue\n\n        if any(p.startswith(specs_prefix) for p in touched):\n            cls = \"amend\" if approval_seen else \"spec\"\n            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": cls})\n            if cls == \"amend\":\n                operator_acts += 1\n            continue\n\n        rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"transport\"})\n        operator_acts += 1\n\n    # issue #137: the same set attavo stops counts, from the same reader\n    # (item_stops) -- not a second, independent count kept in sync by\n    # hand. One non-pass record per row, whatever its stage; a gate\n    # refusal is included the same as a non-pass build or verify record.\n    stops = len(item_stops(root, m, item_id)[\"rows\"])\n\n    summary = {\"operator_acts\": operator_acts, \"product_acts\": product_acts,\n              \"executor_commits\": executor_commits, \"stops\": stops, \"since\": since}\n    return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": rows, \"summary\": summary}\n\n\ndef cmd_ledger(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n    positional = [a for a in argv if a != \"--json\"]\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo ledger: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    if positional:\n        item_ids = [positional[0]]\n    else:\n        records_root = root / records_rel\n        item_ids = (sorted((p.name for p in records_root.iterdir() if p.is_dir()))\n                   if records_root.is_dir() else [])\n\n    ledgers = [item_ledger(root, m, item_id) for item_id in item_ids]\n\n    if as_json:\n        if positional:\n            print(json.dumps(ledgers[0], indent=2))\n        else:\n            print(json.dumps({\"items\": ledgers}, indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    for entry in ledgers:\n        print(f\"attavo ledger: item {entry['item']}\")\n        for row in entry[\"rows\"]:\n            note = f\"  ({row['note']})\" if \"note\" in row else \"\"\n            print(f\"  {row['sha'][:12]}  {row['identity']:<32}  {row['class']}{note}\")\n        s = entry[\"summary\"]\n        print(f\"  operator acts: {s['operator_acts']}  product acts: {s['product_acts']}  \"\n             f\"executor commits: {s['executor_commits']}  stops: {s['stops']}  \"\n             f\"since: {s['since']}\")\n    if not ledgers:\n        print(f\"attavo ledger: no item found under {records_rel}\")\n    return 0\n\n\n# --- stops: every non-pass record by class, provenance, and answerer\n# (issue #129) ---\n\ndef item_stops(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"{\"item\", \"rows\", \"totals\"}: one row per non-pass build or verify\n    record (STOP_STAGES), plus every refused spec-gate record (issue\n    #133), class \"gate\" (issue #137) -- read from status and refusal\n    rather than a stop field spec-gate records never carry (gate_stop\n    synthesizes it) -- under item_id, whatever the record's own\n    record_version -- a record too old to carry stop at all still gets\n    a row, its class printed as the doctor's own phrase for it.\n\n    The answerer, a closed choice: \"counsel:<verdict>\" when\n    counsel_record_for finds a counsel record naming this exact stage and\n    number -- the product's own answer, which wins over whatever the stop\n    itself says, since a counseled stop was already read once; failing\n    that, \"person\" for class question (a person's to answer, not a\n    guard's); failing that, \"guard\" for a class in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES\n    (a guard's own rejection needed no further reading); anything else\n    -- no-cause, unclassed, or no stop at all -- is \"none\": nobody has\n    answered it yet.\"\"\"\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n    by_class = {c: 0 for c in stop_class_enum()}\n    by_answerer: dict[str, int] = {}\n    before_stop_was_recorded = 0\n    rows: list[dict] = []\n\n    def add_row(stage: str, n: int, stop: dict | None) -> None:\n        nonlocal before_stop_was_recorded\n        name = f\"{stage}-{n:02d}\"\n        marker = item_records_dir / f\"{name}.filed\"\n        filed_issue = marker.read_text() if marker.is_file() else None\n        counsel = counsel_record_for(item_records_dir, stage, n)\n\n        if counsel is not None:\n            answerer = f\"counsel:{counsel.get('verdict')}\"\n        elif stop and stop.get(\"class\") == \"question\":\n            answerer = \"person\"\n        elif stop and stop.get(\"class\") in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES:\n            answerer = \"guard\"\n        else:\n            answerer = \"none\"\n\n        if stop:\n            cls, provenance, detail = (stop.get(\"class\"), stop.get(\"provenance\"),\n                                      stop.get(\"detail\"))\n            if cls in by_class:\n                by_class[cls] += 1\n        else:\n            cls, provenance, detail = \"before stop was recorded\", None, None\n            before_stop_was_recorded += 1\n\n        by_answerer[answerer] = by_answerer.get(answerer, 0) + 1\n        rows.append({\"item\": item_id, \"record\": name, \"class\": cls,\n                    \"provenance\": provenance, \"detail\": detail,\n                    \"answerer\": answerer, \"filed_issue\": filed_issue})\n\n    if item_records_dir.is_dir():\n        for stage in STOP_STAGES:\n            for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_records_dir, stage).items()):\n                if rec.get(\"status\") == \"pass\":\n                    continue\n                add_row(stage, n, rec.get(\"stop\"))\n        for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_records_dir, \"spec\").items()):\n            if rec.get(\"status\") != \"refused\":\n                continue\n            add_row(\"spec\", n, gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\")))\n\n    totals = {\"by_class\": by_class, \"by_answerer\": by_answerer,\n             \"before_stop_was_recorded\": before_stop_was_recorded}\n    return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": rows, \"totals\": totals}\n\n\ndef cmd_stops(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n    positional = [a for a in argv if a != \"--json\"]\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo stops: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    if positional:\n        item_ids = [positional[0]]\n    else:\n        records_root = root / records_rel\n        item_ids = (sorted((p.name for p in records_root.iterdir() if p.is_dir()))\n                   if records_root.is_dir() else [])\n\n    reports = [item_stops(root, m, item_id) for item_id in item_ids]\n\n    if as_json:\n        if positional:\n            print(json.dumps(reports[0], indent=2))\n        else:\n            print(json.dumps({\"items\": reports}, indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    for entry in reports:\n        print(f\"attavo stops: item {entry['item']}\")\n        for row in entry[\"rows\"]:\n            filed = f\"  filed: {row['filed_issue'].strip()}\" if row[\"filed_issue\"] else \"\"\n            print(f\"  {row['record']:<10} {row['class']:<24} {row['provenance'] or '-':<10} \"\n                 f\"{row['answerer']:<16}{filed}\")\n        t = entry[\"totals\"]\n        print(f\"  by class: {t['by_class']}\")\n        print(f\"  by answerer: {t['by_answerer']}\")\n        print(f\"  before stop was recorded: {t['before_stop_was_recorded']}\")\n    if not reports:\n        print(f\"attavo stops: no item found under {records_rel}\")\n    return 0\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    if not argv or argv[0] in (\"-h\", \"--help\"):\n        print(__doc__.strip())\n        return 0 if argv else 2\n    if argv[0] == \"doctor\":\n        return cmd_doctor(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"spec-gate\":\n        return cmd_spec_gate(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"approve\":\n        return cmd_approve(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"approval-status\":\n        return cmd_approval_status(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"build\":\n        return cmd_build(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"verify\":\n        return cmd_verify(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"file-findings\":\n        return cmd_file_findings(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"file-stops\":\n        return cmd_file_stops(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"counsel\":\n        return cmd_counsel(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"record-only\":\n        return cmd_record_only(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"attest\":\n        return cmd_attest(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"drive\":\n        return cmd_drive(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"ledger\":\n        return cmd_ledger(argv[1:])\n    if argv[0] == \"stops\":\n        return cmd_stops(argv[1:])\n    print(f\"attavo: unknown subcommand {argv[0]!r}; only doctor, spec-gate, approve, \"\n          f\"approval-status, build, verify, file-findings, file-stops, counsel, record-only, \"\n          f\"attest, drive, ledger, stops exist at this commit\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return 2\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1016,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1016,"newLines":8,"lines":["         stage, nn_text = marker.stem.rsplit(\"-\", 1)","         nn = int(nn_text)","         events = _events_path_for(root, stage, nn)","-        log, last_at = _events_tail(events)","-        age = _seconds_since(last_at or info.get(\"at\"))","+        log = _events_tail(events)","+        age = _seconds_since_last_event(events, info.get(\"at\"))","         pid, host = info.get(\"pid\"), info.get(\"host\")","         if invocation_alive(info):","             if age is None or age <= bound:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
