{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Gj474ME4nfg7pQoazWCc7","type":"tool_result","content":"1901:def stage_events_dir(root: Path) -> Path:\n1902-    \"\"\"<git-dir>/attavo, absolute -- <checkout>/.git/attavo for an\n1903-    ordinary checkout, <main-repo>/.git/worktrees/<name>/attavo for a\n1904-    linked worktree (issue #140). Outside the working tree either way,\n1905-    so a file written here never appears in `git status` in root and is\n1906-    never at risk of being staged and committed by the executor; the\n1907-    screen's seam finds it the same way, with the same command, in its\n1908-    own worktree.\"\"\"\n1909-    git_dir = Path(git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\").strip())\n1910-    events_dir = git_dir / \"attavo\"\n1911-    events_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n1912-    return events_dir\n1913-\n1914-\n1915:def append_event(events_path: Path, kind: str, text: str) -> None:\n1916-    \"\"\"One {at, kind, text} JSON line appended to events_path and flushed\n1917-    at once (open-write-close, not a kept handle) -- the screen tails\n1918-    this file while the stage is still running, so a line held in a\n1919-    buffer is a line the feed does not move on. text is collapsed to one\n1920-    line and capped at EVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS: a tool result can be a whole\n1921-    file, and the feed renders lines, not files.\"\"\"\n1922-    line = {\"at\": now_iso(), \"kind\": kind,\n1923-            \"text\": \" \".join(text.split())[:EVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS]}\n1924-    with events_path.open(\"a\") as fh:\n1925-        fh.write(json.dumps(line) + \"\\n\")\n1926-\n1927-\n1928-def cmd_build(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n1929-    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n1930-    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d","uuid":"2b2e0933-3868-4af6-b186-3eccdc6a966c","timestamp":"2026-09-17T20:04:18.841Z","tool_use_r